INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(2,'Most impressive, $N... the claw of Sharptalon could not have been easy to get!  The Ashenvale Hunt goes well for you!$B$BSharptalon had long terrorized the peons from the lumber camps near its path as they tried to travel here to Splintertree Post.  No doubt once the word gets out that it was you who put down the beast, many rousing songs of your bravery will be heard at campfires and lumber mills across Ashenvale!',70862),
(7,'Well done, citizen.  Those kobolds are thieves and cowards, but in large numbers they pose a threat to us.  And the humans of Stormwind do not need another threat.$B$BFor defeating them, you have my gratitude.',70790),
(8,'Oh? A letter? Wonderful news! I\'ve been waiting on word from my dear old mother in Deathknell. Such a saint, she is. I wonder how she\'s holding up.$B$BWhat? Too cheery? Not buying it, are you?$B$BWell, get lost then... it\'s really no business who the letter\'s from anyway. Go on! Get lost!$B$BCome back when you\'ve got some coin to spend... loafer.$B$BNext thing you know, you\'ll be coming back to rest after a long days adventure or some stupid thing like that.',70862),
(9,'Good work, friend.  You have earned your pay well.  Who knows, perhaps Westfall will prosper once again.',70862),
(11,'I see you\'ve been busy!  You have our thanks, $N.',70862),
(12,'Well done, $N.  My scout witnessed your valiant acts.  You are proving yourself quite well so far.',70862),
(13,'Your worth to The People\'s Militia has been validated by your brave acts thus far.',70862),
(14,'When I left the tainted lands of Lordaeron I returned to a grim state of affairs here in my homeland.  But there is hope for Westfall yet.  As proven by your valor in battle, it is obvious to me that you serve our cause with honor.  It is with great pride that I induct thee into The People\'s Militia.  May the Light shine upon you.',70862),
(15,'I don\'t like hearing of all these kobolds in our mine.  No good can come of this.  Here, take this as payment, and when you\'re ready, speak to me again.  I would like you to go back to the mines one more time...',70790),
(18,'Back with some bandanas, I see.  The Stormwind Army appreciates your help.',70790),
(20,'That makes for a lot fewer orcs to worry about, thanks.',70450),
(21,'Once again, you have earned my respect, and the gratitude of the Stormwind Army.  There may yet be kobolds in the mine, but I will marshal others against them.  We have further tasks for you.',70790),
(22,'These are just perfect, $N!  Thank you so much.  Farmer Saldean and I are going to feast tonight.  And here is a little something for you, for the hard work.  You didn\'t think I was going to let a $c like you go hungry, did you?',70862),
(23,'Ah, the paw of Ursangous!  Your skill is impressive, $c; he is credited with numerous kills.  The crescent on his paw is no doubt a sign that he was trained by the night elves that skulk about Ashenvale.  Ursangous is... was one of the mightiest bears you\'d find in these parts.  To have bested such a creature is a testament to your will and resolve.$B$BYour ancestors would be proud!',70862),
(24,'A victory for $N in the Ashenvale Hunt!  Well done - the head of Shadumbra is a fitting trophy to claim for such an impressive fight, no doubt.$B$BShadumbra\'s savagery was well known throughout the post here.  Any trip to the west, especially on foot trying to get out to the Zoram Strand, was wrought with danger because of this tiger.  Thanks to you, this danger has abated.',70862),
(25,'Yeah, I heard that someone tore up the lake out there like a dust devil through the Barrens.  From the sound of it too, we might be able to set up a possible observation area out there to keep an eye on our Alliance friends.  Well, that is if we can keep it on the down low...$B$BLooks like you ended up being quite useful after all; the transports between here and Stonetalon should have an easier time of it.  Take this - you\'ve earned it.',70862),
(27,'Salutations, young $c; the time has come for you to know our aquatic form.  It is one that lets you move freely and indefinitely through water.  You will find this aspect a useful tool and a blessing... but it is one that must be earned before it is mastered.$B$BYou will face two trials to overcome.  The first will test your ability to work in water under pressure.  The second will test your resolve to understand the aspects of the form itself.$B$BStand ready, as the time of testing is now upon us.',70790),
(28,'Well now, it looks like yet another $c has successfully completed the Trial of the Lake!  Well done, my young friend - well done.$B$BAs I\'ve said, my name is Tajarri.  It is my duty and my privilege to serve as a warden for Moonglade, and specifically this shrine.  Keeper Remulos guides the Cenarion Circle in preservation of nature and balance, and his shrine serves as a lasting tribute to such.  By using the bauble here, it serves as a nod to the importance of this place within the Circle.',70790),
(30,'You\'ve completed the Trial of the Sea Lion, $N - congratulations.$B$BEach task in acquiring the pendant shows that both agility and endurance are necessary to act in harmony with what you desire to do underwater.  Neither can exist without the other, and both cannot be done without your willingness to embrace the aspect of the sea lion.$B$BRemember these lessons well, and count on them once you have gained your aquatic form.',70790),
(31,'Very impressive, $N.  Your ancestors would be pleased with your progress!  You\'re ready to learn your aquatic form, and it is my pleasure to teach it to you.$B$BAlso, in recognition of your achievement during the two trials, I give you this item.  I hope you\'ll find it to be a welcome addition to your gear as a protector of nature and a keeper of the balance.',70790),
(33,'You\'ve been busy!  I can\'t wait to cook up that wolf meat...$B$BI have some things here you might want - take your pick!',70790),
(34,'Finally the menace is laid to rest!  Thank you, $N, you have done me a great service.  The garden shall be in full bloom this season!',70862),
(35,'Yes, murlocs have settled in and around the streams of eastern Elwynn.  We don\'t know why they are here, but they are aggressive and at least semi-intelligent.',70790),
(36,'That Verna was always such a sweet lass.  We\'ll miss her here in Westfall but between you and me, she\'s a city girl at heart and Stormwind will suit her just fine.  But enough gossip!  Now we can make Westfall Stew!',70862),
(37,'Although much has been stripped from the corpse, strewn nearby is a medallion with the words: "Footman Malakai Stone" etched upon it.',70790),
(38,'That Okra will thicken up this broth nicely!  Now we just add the Stringy Vulture Meat, a few Murloc Eyes and those delicious Goretusk Snouts.  And we\'re done!  For all your help, $N, I want you to take today\'s first batch of Westfall Stew!',70862),
(39,'Hmm, this news is troubling.  Already our defenses are stretched thin, and losing Rolf and Malakai to those murlocs put us in an even worse position.$B$BIf things don\'t improve, there will be fighting in Goldshire by the week\'s end!',70790),
(40,'Yes, I spoke with Remy.  I respect him as a merchant, though all reports of Murlocs to the east have been sketchy at best.$B$BYour concerns are noted, but unless I receive a military report of a murloc threat, we can\'t afford to send more troops east.',70790),
(45,'You find around the neck of the corpse a metal medallion inscribed with the words "Footman Rolf Hartford."',70790),
(46,'You have the fins?  Great!  Marshal Dughan is anxious about the Murloc situation in eastern Elwynn, and I\'d like to tell him that it\'s becoming under control.$B$BYour actions have helped realize that.',70862),
(47,'Thanks for the dust, $N.  Here\'s your cash, and...here is a token from associates of mine.  You might find it useful...useful.',70790),
(52,'Thanks a lot for the help, $N.  Something in the forest must be making these animals so bold.$B$BWhatever it is, I hope it stays there.',70790),
(54,'Well, it says here that you\'ve been awarded Acting Deputy Status with the Stormwind Marshals.  Congratulations.$B$BAnd good luck - keeping Elwynn safe is no picnic... what with most the army busy doing who knows what for who knows which noble!$B$BIt\'s hard to keep track of politics in these dark days...',70790),
(59,'Ah, thank you for the marker.  Please feel free to pick your choice of armor.$B$BLuck to you, brave $c.  And may this armor serve you well.',70790),
(60,'You were busy hunting kobolds, were you?  Thanks for the candles, $N, and here\'s your reward...',70790),
(61,'Here is your payment ... and while you\'re here, take a look around!  I\'m sure we have a potion or other trinket you\'d find useful.',70790),
(62,'This is bad news.  What\'s next, dragons?!?  We\'ll have to increase our patrols near that mine.  Thanks for your efforts, $N.  And hold a moment... I might have another task for you.',70790),
(63,'You place the bracers atop the brazier and then pour the remaining drops of Brine\'s potion into the flame. The drops crackle as they hit the flame and you begin to incant the simple words Islen taught you....',70862),
(64,'My watch!  Thank you so much, kind sir! $B$BWe are but poor farmers and we have lost our land but please accept this reward as a token of our appreciation.',70862),
(65,'So, Stoutmantle sent you?  Well, I owe him.',70862),
(66,'Ah so Madame Eva sent you. . . .',70450),
(71,'You have confirmed my fears, $N.  The murlocs are a threat we cannot ignore.',70790),
(76,'Kobolds at the Jasperlode Mine, you say?  Curses!  The situation is worsening by the minute!$B$BThank you for the report, $N.  But I wish that the news you brought was good news.',70790),
(83,'Ah, these are nice bandanas, if a little rough...$B$BHere you are!',70790),
(84,'Mm, yum!  This pie is the best!$B$BI think my memory is coming back to me...',70862),
(85,'You lost a what?  Well I didn\'t take no necklace, because I ain\'t no thief!$B$BI might know who did but...<grin>...I\'m too hungry to remember.',70862),
(86,'Though this wild boar meat is tough, simmer it enough and it sure does make for some tasty pie!',70862),
(96,'This is the proof I asked for. You\'ve done well, $N.$B$BI am pleased to be the first to congratulate you and give you this... your water totem.$B$BUse it well, and good luck.$B$BYour next test will not be for some time, so learn your lessons well. Pure water will not only give life back to those who are injured, but can have many other effects. I suggest you seek out a $c trainer when you have the time. They might have other spells for you to learn.',70862),
(99,'Your persistence is commendable.  With the knowledge you helped me gather, Arugal will fall and his reckless magic shall be undone.  Cheers to you, $N.',70862),
(100,'Thanks to you. Thanks to the shamans.$B$BCorruption ebbs but life continues to wane. Up to shamans to protect life.',70862),
(102,'Well done, $N.  With valiant adventurers such as yourself fighting alongside The People\'s Militia, Westfall just might return to the prosperous breadbasket it once was.  Please accept this in recognition of your tireless efforts.',70862),
(106,'Ah!  I can\'t stand us being apart.  I have to see her!!',70862),
(109,'Ah, so my friend sent you here?  How kind.  $B$BWell the Stormwind Monarchy has abandoned our cause.  Now it is up to the People\'s Militia to keep the land free from corruption.  If our cause interests you, I can put your combat skills to use in the name of freedom.',70862),
(111,'While our families are feuding, Tommy Joe and Maybell don\'t have much of a future, but... maybe we can get them together for just a little while.$B$BHm, what can we do...',70862),
(117,'Hops and Barley, yeast and malt $BThe taste-buds feel a virtual assault, $BNo need to plead, no need to beg $BFor Thunderbrew Lager comes in a keg!',70862),
(120,'At ease, $c.$B$BMagistrate Solomon is a noble leader.  His words carry great weight with me.  I shall seek the counsel of the King and make the situation clear to him.  Assure the good judge that he has the Stormwind Army\'s support.  Reinforcements will be sent as soon as word is given from His Majesty.',70862),
(121,'Thank you for your time, $c.  For your service to Lakeshire and Stormwind I reward you with these coins.$B$BNow if you\'ll excuse me, I find this correspondence somewhat of a mystery.  Something is amiss in our Kingdom.  I fear this is the beginning of conflict, not the end.',70862),
(123,'Hm... I have heard of this "Collector" but I don\'t know whom he\'s working for.  Thank you for the schedule.  It will help us solve this mystery.',70862),
(124,'Thank you for all your help, $N.',70450),
(127,'Pleasure doin\' business with you, matey!',70450),
(129,'Thanks, I could really use the meal.  Guarding Lakeshire from the orcs and gnolls is tough work!',70862),
(130,'You need a bouquet of flowers?  You haven\'t been in town very long...have you already found for yourself a sweetheart here?$B$BI know I shouldn\'t pry, but it\'s nice to see that love is in the air... especially in dangerous times like these.',70862),
(131,'Oh, those are lovely!  I can\'t wait to put them in some water!$B$BBut...these are Martie\'s favorite flowers.  Parker didn\'t have you go to that jealous vixen for this bouquet, did he?  You didn\'t tell her who they were for, did you?  If you did, then it wouldn\'t surprise me if she poisoned them.$B$BOh, but it\'s not your fault.  Thank you, and here\'s your meal.',70862),
(132,'Bah!  I should have let that scoundrel rot when I had the chance.  But this information is crucial.  Good work.',70862),
(135,'This matter might be more complex than Stoutmantle realizes.',70862),
(136,'The footlocker slowly creaks open.  Sand and water seem to be its only contents. But wait!  A small crab scurries out with a clue to the treasure in his claws!',70862),
(138,'Good work, treasure hunter!',70862),
(141,'Edwin VanCleef... I know the name well.  To think that a man so industrious and talented could turn into such a scoundrel unnerves me.  I\'ll need further proof before I believe this.',70862),
(142,'This is indeed firm proof that VanCleef is in charge.  Now all we need to know is where the Defias gang is hiding out.$B$BWe\'ve had a stroke of luck while you were gone.  We captured a thief trying to steal Saldean\'s wagon.  He has promised to lead us to the hideout in exchange for his life.  I want you to defend the traitor so he can reveal the hideout.  Return to me once you have uncovered the location.',70862),
(147,'You found him?  Well done, $N.  He won\'t be "collecting" from the Elwynn Mines again!$B$BAnd this ring you found is interesting... it\'s a membership ring for the old Stonemason\'s Guild in Stormwind.  Why would a lowly thief have an artisan guild ring, and why are the Defias Thieves collecting money from our mines?$B$BDifficult questions.  I hope one day we\'ll have answers.',70862),
(150,'Well done, $N.  I hope you didn\'t have too much trouble with those murlocs.$B$BIt\'s strange seeing them so far from the sea.  I wonder if they\'re here because they\'re running from something...',70450),
(151,'Thank you so much, $N!  Poor Old Blanchy will be so happy!',70862),
(153,'Nice work, $r.  Please accept one of these items as payment for all your hard work.',70862),
(155,'Most excellent, $N!  VanCleef is as good as ours now that we know where he is hiding.',70862),
(156,'Good,  you got the rot blossoms.  And I\'ll tell Althea Ebonlocke of the Night Watch that you were killing skeletons.$B$BKeeping the people of Darkshire safe is a grim burden for the Night Watch, and news that others are helping stem the tide of fiends in Duskwood is welcome news indeed.',70450),
(166,'$N, your bravery is remarkable.  The People\'s Militia thanks you for your service to the people of Westfall.  With VanCleef dead, this marks the beginning of the end for the Defias Brotherhood.  Hopefully some day soon peace will once again grace the plains of this fair land.$B$BI salute you, Sir!',70862),
(176,'Hah!  Well done!  I was starting to think no one would take down that monster!$B$BHere you are, $N.  And thanks - that Gnoll was giving me a headache the size of Blackrock Spire!',70790),
(184,'Loads of thanks, $N!  As I was saying, these parts aren\'t fit for honest folk anymore, but if things get better, then this deed will let us reclaim our land.$B$BI don\'t have much to offer you, but here -- take this.',70862),
(214,'Well done, $N!  On behalf of The People\'s Militia I salute you for your efforts.  Soon we will return this land to the people with help from brave souls like you.',70862),
(216,'Well done $c, well done!  I will continue to send forces to thin out the furbolg, but I can at least count on a different path that will be free of Alliance entanglements.  The Horde conquest of Ashenvale is now in full swing!$B$BYou\'ve earned your pay this day, hero.  I salute you!',70862),
(217,'Most excellent, $N!  You have brought hope to Loch Modan.  With Grawmug dead, we stand a better chance of seeing the Troggs eliminated from the land.',70338),
(220,'Ah, a vial of water created and blessed by Brine, and gathered by you, no less.$B$BThe liquid in this vial will be key in creating a sapta for you, but also used in one other task.$B$BThe sapta I create for you should be used to see the water spirits at the shrine in Silverpine Forest, south of the Undercity. The remaining drops, well, the remaining drops I will tell you about if you feel you are ready.$B$BAre you prepared for one more journey, $N?',70862),
(224,'Well done, $N!  You demonstrated uncanny courage on the battlefield.  Our war against the Troggs will be won with efforts such as yours.  You have served King Magni well.$B$BIf you fancy yourself well-suited for this kind of adventuring, I suggest you speak with Mountaineer Gravelgaw.  The Captain has him assigned to a rough patrol that I am sure he can use some help with.  Check with Gravelgaw just inside the tower.',70338),
(235,'Welcome to the new frontier, $N.  Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young $c like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle.  Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.$B$BYour presence here tells me that you\'ve come to learn more about the hunt.  Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.',70338),
(237,'You accomplished your mission well, $r.  The King himself would be proud.$B$BThe reinforcements promised to us never showed, however.  Apparently the Alliance front is a sea of crimson from the blood of our fallen brethren.  The news of the losses leaves a bitter taste in one\'s mouth.  But we must not let their deaths go for naught.  We must rally in these grim times and bring glory back to the Alliance.$B$BSpeak with Mountaineer Wallbang for reassignment.  You\'re needed now more than ever.',70338),
(239,'Marshall Dughan sent you, eh?  Well you\'re not from the army, but if Dughan sent you then that\'s good enough for me!$B$BOur situation is, to say the least, a stressed one.  I hope you can give us a hand.',70790),
(244,'There are Redridge gnolls that close to Elwynn??  They may be poised to advance into our homeland.  Soon the people of Lakeshire may not be the only humans under siege!$B$BHere is your pay, though you bring us dire news.  And it comes at a bad time, for we are ill equipped to deal with it.',70862),
(246,'<Deputy Feldon listens to your report...>$B$BThere\'s a sizable force of gnolls encamped there, and from what you tell me they are tough ones.  It must not have been easy for you to gather this intelligence.$B$BHere you are, $N.  We are grateful for your aid.$B$BAnd if you haven\'t already done so, speak with Marshal Marris and Magistrate Solomon within Lakeshire.  Our situation grows ever more desperate - those two will have need of you I\'m sure.',70862),
(247,'$N, you have slain all three beasts that comprise the Ashenvale Hunt.  You have brought me adequate proof of their demise; there is no question of your strength and tenacity.  The blood of a hunter streaks through your veins, and you should be commended!$B$BPlease, accept this bauble as a sign of congratulations on your mighty deeds done in Ashenvale for the Horde today.  May your ancestors watch over you!',70862),
(263,'I knew the second I laid eyes on you, $N, that you would make Ironforge proud.  You have served King Magni well.  Now that you\'ve proven yourself to be such a loyal aid to the Kingdom, perhaps you should talk with the Captain to see if he\'ll entrust you with a higher detail.$B$BI salute you, $N.',70338),
(264,'You place the worthless pendant on the grave, and the gemstone within the setting seems to dull noticeably.$B$BAs you stand to leave, you look down at the pendant; it lies lifelessly over the hands of the relief sculpted into the top of the coffin. Your thoughts are interrupted by a stiff, cool breeze passing over the Sepulcher. For a moment everything around you is silent. ',70790),
(267,'I am quite impressed, $N.  You have done the Dwarven race a great favor by defending our lands.  King Magni Bronzebeard himself would be proud!',70338),
(307,'Did you see a lot of Kobolds in there?  I can\'t wait for the order to clear them out of the mine.  The thought of their grimy hands clawing around our mine makes my stomach rumble!',70338),
(308,'For me? You\'re a true hero, $N!',70338),
(310,'You quickly place Marleth\'s barrel of Barleybrew Scalder among the Thunderbrew barrels.',70338),
(311,'Not bad, $N! Did you have a hard time getting past their guard?$B$BNo matter--many thanks, and if you\'re ever in need of stout with a kick, don\'t forget the Barleybrews!',70338),
(315,'Great!  I can\'t wait to use these in some of my recipes.  There\'s one in particular I think it\'ll work great in...',70338),
(332,'Ah, so you\'ve seen Renato?  Well here you are, sir.  A bottle of our special pinot noir.  You\'ll not find its equal in all of Azeroth!',70291),
(333,'It says here that Harlan\'s business is booming.  That\'s good news, but I wonder why people have need of all that armor.  I\'ve heard nothing of open war...is there something the nobles aren\'t telling us?$B$BWell, thank you for bringing the request.  Here\'s your payment, and I\'ll see to it that Harlan gets his supplies.',70291),
(353,'Aha!  So Grimand finally finished my axe!  I can\'t wait to try it against some troggs and kobolds!$B$BMany thanks, $N.  It was a long distance to travel for this delivery.   Here are some coins for your efforts.',70862);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(354,'Revenge has a sweet taste, don\'t you think?  When you destroyed the Agamands, did you catch any hint of free will within them?  I hope so.  I hope they knew fear before they were smashed into oblivion.$B$BIt is a foolish hope, I know.  But it is a hope I foster nonetheless.',70862),
(355,'Coleman speaks well of you, $N, telling of your successful forays into the Agamand Mills.$B$BThe Forsaken have need of your talents once again...',70862),
(356,'Very good. Your efforts do much to keep the Scourge at bay. A commendation will be sent to my superior, Executor Zygand.',70862),
(357,'Very good, $N.  I will study this book and determine the identity of that lich.  You have served your Queen well.$B$B<Bethor opens the book and stares intently at its glowing pages...>$B$BAstonishing!  The book you retrieved belongs to no one other than Gunther Arcanus!$B$BGunther was a skilled Necromancer in life; he and I were friends and comrades-in-arms, before the Plague.  And judging from his book he has grown even more powerful in death.$B$BHis skills would be a great boon to us.',70790),
(358,'Expertly done, $N.  The Scourge are mistaken if they think they can use those corpses against us, and the fluid you gathered from the Rot Hide slaves will be studied by our Apothecaries.  It may have secrets we can use against them.$B$BAs I said, well done.  But our struggle continues, and the conflict will surely offer you more chances to prove your worth to the Forsaken.',70862),
(359,'Magistrate Sevren wants a report?  Very well: the defenders at The Bulwark are holding the majority of the Scourge at bay, but some do slip through on occasion.$B$BWe have seen sporadic Scourge activity east of this station, with a concentration around the Balnir Farmstead.',70862),
(360,'It is troubling to hear of the Scourge slipping past the Bulwark.  The Lich King and his minions are ceaseless in their assaults.$B$BBut we will not give in.  He will not take us again!',70862),
(361,'Oh...my poor Thurman!  I begged him to leave Agamand Mills with me and my father, but his family loyalty was too strong!  And I knew it!  I just knew it that Brand meant him harm!!  Oh, curse this Plague, and the Scourge!$B$B<Yvette\'s face then smoothes and grows cold.>$B$BBut regrets are for the weak.  As a Forsaken, I have new goals and love is not one of them.  I would thank you for delivering this letter, for I had wondered what happened to my past love.$B$BBut that life is over.  Forever.',70862),
(362,'Thank you.  Devlin\'s bones will rest nicely on my mantle.$B$BIf my cold heart can find warmth, it is in knowing that the Agamands are destroyed.  They failed me and my family when the Plague came - now I swear I will smash their remains under my heel!',70862),
(363,'Another of the walking dead, hm? Must have been quite a shock, waking up in the crypt with only the cold and Mordo to greet you...$B$BI see the confusion on your face. Let me try to explain our... situation... to you.$B$BWe have been freed from the control of the Lich King by our new leader, Lady Sylvanas. The Dark Lady guides us in our war against the hated Scourge and the holdouts of humanity who dog our every step.',70862),
(364,'It is unfortunate that the Scourge cannot be brought into the fold, their large numbers would be useful in the battles ahead.$B$BBut they will not join us, so we have no choice but to destroy them.',70862),
(365,'You have performed your bidding well, young $c.  You are proving yourself to be quite an asset to The Dark Lady\'s army.',70862),
(366,'My book?!?  So you were the thief who stole it!$B$BBut...what is this new enchantment upon it...Bethor?  He is in  Lordaeron?$B$BIf he still exists, then perhaps he too escaped from the Lich King\'s grasp...',70790),
(367,'You have done well $N, and I thank you for your efforts.',70862),
(368,'The scales are perfect, $N. Exactly what I needed for this concoction.',70862),
(369,'Ah, this venom will do perfectly, $N.  Everything else has been added to my concoction and boiled down.  Finally, I am ready to try this new deadly agent!',70790),
(370,'Captain Perrine\'s death will undoubtedly please The Dark Lady.  You have performed your duty well, $c.',70790),
(371,'Captain Vachon\'s death will slow down the Scarlet Crusade\'s advancement in Tirisfal quite a bit.  But other threats loom.',70450),
(372,'You have done extremely well, $c.  With ruthless fighters like you conquering in the name of The Forsaken our race is one step closer to defeating Arthas once and for all.  I have a good feeling about you, comrade.',70790),
(373,'Edwin VanCleef, you say? I would as much expect a letter from my dead grandmother... So you\'ve killed him then? Pardon me in saying, but I\'m somewhat surprised. He was a peerless fighter in his younger years. Let\'s see what he finds the need to write to me about after so many years.$B$B<Baros peruses the letter.>$B$BEdwin... I see the years haven\'t changed you a bit, an idealist as ever, and a romantic. He doesn\'t care who he hurts, $N. Revenge has consumed him. But then, I\'m not sure I can blame him.',70862),
(374,'Varimathras would be proud.  You serve your leaders well, $c.',70790),
(375,'I appreciate your efforts, $N.  May Sylvanas recognize your bravery one day. . . .',70862),
(376,'Thank you, $N. This armor should help you out.$B$BHopefully, it should do you more good than the last one to wear it...',70862),
(380,'Hmm, well, it\'s a start. It\'ll take a few weeks or months to fully clean out the infestation. After that, we\'ll have to get down there with some torches to burn away the webbing.$B$BYou\'ve done your duty well, $N, I\'m sure I can find something else for you to do.',70862),
(381,'If only they listened to reason, eh, $N? Perhaps we could sit them down for reasonable discourse... ha!$B$BLight-blinded fools.',70862),
(382,'Hmm... Let\'s see what you\'ve got...$B$B<He begins to rifle through the documents you recovered.>$B$BSome news of their exploits against us... Worthless. Scouting reports... New orders, "Continue to build up a camp near the ruined city..." Nothing we didn\'t know already... Ah, what\'s this? A map of the dispositions of some of their field commanders and agents! We can use this.',70862),
(383,'Yes, this is very good. You\'ve done well in obtaining this information, $N. Hmm... names of the officers in the Tirisfal Glades...$B$BImagine the blow we could deal to the morale of those bloody zealots if we were to kill their leaders in one swift strike.',70862),
(389,'What in the Light do you want? Can\'t you see we have a crisis here?$B$BBazil Thredd?! Why would you want to speak with that bastard? How am I supposed to know you\'re not one of his cronies, come down to help with his bloody riot? If all the blasted cells weren\'t open, I might throw you in one for a while!',70862),
(398,'Maggot Eye\'s dastardly acts have finally been avenged.  Maybe your acts of valor will send a clear message to those who wish to bring harm to our people.  On behalf of the town of Brill I thank you, $N.',70862),
(399,'Oh, thank you, $N! It\'s of no practical use to me, but the sentimental value... Needless to say, thank you for bringing this to me... at some cost to your own well-being, not to mention the time it took to go all the way down to Westfall. You have my gratitude, and have this as a token of my thanks.',70862),
(404,'Well done.  I regret not being there to see you smash those $r into rotting pulp!',70862),
(405,'Ah, you are the agent sent by Magistrate Sevren.  Then yes, your business with me is crucial.$B$BI trust Sevren has mustered someone suitable for my task...but we shall see.',70862),
(407,'By the Light!  Finally some food!  Sweet, sweet pumpkin. . . .',70862),
(408,'Your actions struck a telling blow against the Scourge.  And your victory will not go unnoticed - not by the Forsaken, nor by our enemies.$B$BContinue the struggle as we all do, $N, and one day we will drive the Lich King himself from Azeroth!',70790),
(409,'You have defeated Lillith Nefara, proving you are an enemy of the Scourge.  Incredible.$B$BI had believed I was the only $R with free will, but you have shown me there are others who have broken the Lich King\'s domination.',70790),
(410,'You place the Candle of Beckoning upon the table and light it...',70235),
(411,'You convinced him to join us!  You have done a great deed for the Forsaken, $N.  The Dark Lady will be informed.',70235),
(412,'These Gyromechanic Gears and Restabilization Cogs are in perfect accordance with Ozzie\'s schematics for the Recombobulation Device.  Once I add some hydrolubricant to the inner combustion pistons, adjust the crank-o-ratchet and increase of the viscosity of the electrogum gel, the gnomish race will be as good as new.',70338),
(413,'<Mountaineer Barleybrew tastes the Shimmer Stout...>$B$BOh.  Whoa!  This stuff really puts a shine in your eyes.  I feel like I can see in the dark!',70338),
(414,'Now, let me have a taste...$B$BMagni\'s Beard!  This stuff gets your head turning!  And it lightens the limbs, too.$B$BI feel like I can fly!',70338),
(416,'Ugh!  When I asked for those ears I didn\'t realize they\'d smell so bad!$B$BHere\'s your reward, $N.  Well done.',70338),
(418,'Trust me, it seems a lot harder than it looks, but...$B$BOh, I\'ve never known someone to take much interest in the making of sausages, but I\'ll give you the recipe just in case. Here you go, mind you eat them fresh!',70338),
(421,'You have served me well, $c.  It is obvious to me that you will be a worthy aide to me as I prepare to rid Silverpine Forest of Arugal\'s curse.',70862),
(422,'This is precisely the spell I was in search of, $c.  If your dedication to The Dark Lady\'s cause remains infallible you will find you have quite a future amongst The Forsaken.',70862),
(423,'I hope I can acquire enough energy from such a limited sample.  Perhaps I should have had you get more shackles.$B$BNonetheless, you showed great skill in collecting these, $c.',70862),
(424,'Most excellent.  The mine will provide superb resources for our forces as we spread throughout Silverpine and into Azeroth.',70862),
(425,'Ah, thank you.  You have my gratitude, $N.$B$BAnd I will include you in the report I make to my superiors.',70862),
(426,'Your efforts in the war are felt among us, $N.  I will not thank you for doing what is necessary, but the Deathguards of Tirisfal will remember your name.',70862),
(427,'Most excellent, $c.  Your skill in the art of combat is undeniable.',70862),
(428,'You found us!  And not a moment too soon...',70338),
(429,'<Renferrel takes the hearts.>$B$BIt is troubling to hear our Deathstalkers have failed their mission.$B$BLet us hope that these failures are rare.$B$BI\'ll give you the potion in a moment.',70862),
(430,'<Quinn takes the potion and drinks it.>$B$B<A few moments pass in suspenseful silence.>',70862),
(431,'You grab one of the candles and place it in your pack.',70235),
(432,'Well, that makes me feel a little better...$B$BBut I won\'t be happy until they\'re all dead! All of them!',70338),
(433,'It is a start. Hopefully we can take advantage of it, and move some Mountaineers in to secure the area. Then we can begin to restore our infrastructure and get the miners back to work.$B$BThank you for your assistance, $N.',70338),
(435,'Thank you for the aid, $N.  I had feared Erland was overcome by the dangers of Silverpine.  With your help, I see that he has not.',70790),
(437,'I heard of your successful raid against the rot hides, $N, and this essence is proof of Nightlash\'s death.$B$BThe Scourge have lost ground this day.  Your value to the Forsaken grows.',70862),
(438,'Heaped within this boat is a pile of wrapped corpses.  And looking east across Lordamere Lake, an opposing dock on Fenris Isle can be seen.$B$BThe fate of the corpses must lie on Fenris Isle.',70862),
(439,'You say that this ring was worn by a woman, recently killed?$B$BThe only nearby source of such a body would be the mass graves in Tirisfal.  The Rot Hide Gnolls must be taking those corpses to Fenris Isle!',70862),
(440,'A Deliah did live in Brill not long ago.  She was buried in the mass grave but if what you say is true, then the Rot Hide Gnolls must have stolen her body and taken it to Silverpine.$B$BThe Rot Hides, like all the Scourge, must be destroyed.  I trust you are taking steps to make that happen.',70862),
(441,'Yes, this ring was my wife\'s.  Her fate was the fate of all who fail to endure these harsh times.  I feel nothing for her death, nor for the story you tell of her body\'s abduction.$B$BSuch feelings have long since grown cold within me.  But desire does still burn in my dead heart, $N.$B$BDesire for revenge.',70862),
(443,'Very good.  This ichor will help us understand the nature of the rot hides, and may show us their weakness...$B$B...if they have one.',70862),
(444,'This substance is laced with powerful spells, some of which I have not seen for a long, long time...$B$BOne moment -- I must invoke a spell of divination...',70862),
(445,'Ah, how good of Apothecary Johaan to send his research.  With so many new developments here in Silverpine, I nearly forgot about the findings coming out of Lordaeron and Tirisfal Glades.  Which reminds me, I need to get those samples off to the Necropolis soon.$B$BBut you must excuse my rambling.  Extend your stay in Silverpine, $N.  We could use an able bodied $c like you around here.',70790),
(446,'This scroll is laced with powerful magic.  I\'ve never used such forces in a potion ... it will be a powerful mixture, and should serve you well should you attack Thule in his stronghold on Fenris Isle.',70862),
(447,'How good of Apothecary Renferrel to send you to me, $N.  These samples will indeed prove useful to the cause.  I will begin studying their toxic and contaminable properties at once.',70862),
(448,'If what Bethor says is true then Thule Ravenclaw is a force that must be dealt with, and dealt with soon.$B$BTo aid in this task, you may take something from our arsenal here...',70862),
(449,'I hadn\'t accounted for the level of Scourge presence we\'ve seen in Silverpine Forest, nor for the troubles our Deathstalkers have had in their scouting efforts.$B$BYour aid to our Deathstalkers was invaluable, $N.  And you will be commended.',70790),
(450,'Apothecary Berard\'s journal!  Why you are quite brave, $N.  Now let\'s see what Berard was up to before he went mad. . .',70862),
(451,'Such a blow to the Royal Apothecary Society to lose Berard.  But through your hard work and Apothecary Renferrel\'s diligent research Berard\'s studies will still be useful to The Dark Lady\'s plight.$B$BWe are on the cusp of something great here, $N.  If you were not so skilled in the ways of combat I would try to recruit you for membership in the Society.',70862),
(452,'You fought like a true disciple of the Dark Lady, $N.  With the council dead, perhaps we can gain control of this town once and for all and drive Arugal from Shadowfang Keep.  I salute you!',70862),
(456,'You performed your duties well, $N.',70790),
(457,'You have proven your dedication to nature well, $N.  A young $c like yourself has a promising future.',70790),
(458,'I see you found me, young $r.  Melithar is a wise druid to have sent you. But you still have much to learn. I understand your kind enjoys books. Please take one of these to further your education.',70790),
(459,'Your service to the creatures of Shadowglen is worthy of reward, $N.$B$BYou confirmed my fears, however.  If the grells have become tainted by the Fel Moss, one can only imagine what has become of the Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs who once lived here.$B$BShould you find yourself in Dolanaar, able $C, seek out the knowledgeable druid, Athridas Bearmantle.  He shares our concern for the well being of the forest.',70790),
(460,'Thank you, $N.  I had feared the Gnolls destroyed my body.  It is good to know they did not.',70338),
(461,'There we are, it\'s open.  Leave me here.  I spent the best days of my life in this keep, and the thought of resting within its walls gives me comfort.$B$BBe sure to close the alcove tight - I don\'t want those Rot Hides to find me.$B$BOh, and take this.  You\'ve earned it.',70338),
(475,'Thank the forest spirits you are here!  I knew Athridas would sense trouble and send help.',70790),
(476,'By the stars!  This is quite disturbing indeed!',70790),
(477,'<Prying open the lid of the crate, you find an assortment of carefully-packed objects. On the top of the crate lies a bundle of maps, yellowing with age, that appear to depict Silverpine Forest and other parts of western Lordaeron.$B$BUnderneath the maps is a mysterious-looking magical pendant.>',70862),
(478,'Maps and this... pendant, hm? Interesting.$B$BIt is obvious that the Dalaran wizards are interested in Ambermill for some purpose, but still, their aim is hidden to me.$B$BPerhaps Dalar will know something of their use.',70862),
(479,'Dalar has found that the weaving is quite far along, despite the setback.$B$BA wizard of great power is guiding the magic energy. He must be stopped quickly.',70862),
(480,'The magic of the wizards dissipates, and the ley energies fade into dormancy. Your efforts have been fruitful, $N, and we have dealt a major blow to our enemies, and to the overbearing wizards of Dalaran.$B$BWe must be vigilant, however, knowing that source of energy lies so close at hand... Plans must be made for the future.',70338),
(481,'Interesting, more machinations of the Kirin Tor, it would seem. This is a powerful artifact. It was used frequently by powerful wizards of the Kirin Tor to channel magical energies.$B$BThat they are delivering so many to Ambermill indicates that they must be undergoing a project of some magnitude.$B$BI will see if I can pierce their shields and ascertain their intent.',70862),
(482,'Ill news you bring, $N. If Dalar is correct--and I\'ve no reason to believe he isn\'t--we must move quickly.$B$BI must confer with him on our plan of attack. But in the meanwhile we will have to delay their progress.',70862),
(483,'You have succeeded, young $c!  Well done.  And just in time I might add.',70790),
(487,'You have served the good people of Dolanaar and Darnassus well, brave $c.  As a member of the Sentinel force of Teldrassil I salute your efforts.',70790),
(488,'Ha ha!  Well, done indeed.$B$BWho would have ever guessed that I, Zenn Foulhoof, would have a $r to do my bidding?  Certainly not me!  But so it goes... this beloved world of ours is full of surprises.$B$BThree cheers for the naive and gullible!',70790),
(489,'Ah, what a sweet $r!  I knew you would come in handy!',70790),
(491,'...what is this?  Thule had our Woven Wand?  I thought it was lost when our friendship sundered and he sided with the Lich King!$B$BHe must not have invoked its power, for if he had I would have sensed it.  And it is good that he did not use it...$B$BThis is a marvelous find.  You have my gratitude, $N, and will be rewarded.',70338),
(492,'Ah, a drink at last.  I\'m sure it\'s no Rhapsody Malt but I\'ll take anything to whet the old whistle at this point.',70245),
(493,'Ah, most excellent.  Apothecary Renferrel has my utmost respect.  I am anxious to study his work.',70862),
(494,'The raven\'s cry from the west doth beckon?$B$BSuperb news!  Hillsbrad is ripe for attack.  We can carry out our plan of destruction now.  Varimathras will be pleased.',70862),
(496,'These specimens are perfect.  Well, $N, you have managed to bring me the slightest hint of joy on yet another miserable day.  Your efforts are appreciated.',70790),
(498,'So the humans thought to turn our warriors into slaves, did they? We\'ll show them!$B$BIt would seem that they have taken Gol\'dir, our leader, to another location. We must find him and rescue him. But we currently have no clue where he is...$B$BWhen we have a lead, I will be sure to tell you, $N.',70790),
(501,'Superb collecting, $N.',70790),
(509,'Ah, the horrible reek of Mudsnout Blossoms.  At least those filthy Gnolls are good for something.',70862),
(516,'If our scouts and agents continue to procure valuable information such as this, we shall have the Lich King\'s Scourge removed from our lands in no time.',70790),
(527,'At ease, $c.  I see you have returned from battle.  My sources tell me you performed well on the Hillsbrad front.',70790),
(528,'The grip of death is tightening around the town of Hillsbrad.  The battle goes well.',70840);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(529,'Mission accomplished, $c.  And carried out quite skillfully, I might add.',70840),
(530,'Ah, good.  These hands killed my wife, Deliah.  Revenge for her murder was my only care, and you were the instrument of that revenge.$B$BHere, take the ring you returned earlier.  Deliah has been dead to me for so long, her ring is a bauble I no longer care to keep.  Instead, I will keep these hands as a remembrance of my friend\'s betrayal.',70790),
(532,'News of your glories in Hillsbrad traveled fast.  You have done well, $c.',70862),
(533,'Finally, we know where Gol\'dir is being held. The camp in question is not too far from here, and hopefully they will not be as well prepared as they were when they captured us the first time.',70862),
(539,'The Dark Lady will be pleased when she learns that she has a new mine from which she can arm her soldiers.',70862),
(544,'You have done a great service for the Forsaken, $N. These artifacts have been sorely missed.$B$BAnd it is good to hear that Kegan and the other betrayers have found justice.',70862),
(545,'Very good. Thank you, $N.$B$BNow we are free to pay Dalaran a little visit.',70862),
(549,'Excellent, $c. At this rate, the Syndicate pest will be rid from the land in no time.',70790),
(552,'You found it!  Most excellent, $N!',70862),
(556,'These will do nicely.  Although it looks like their magic is faded, it would be best if the Magus\' initial experiments were on inert specimens such as these.$B$BThank you, $N.',70862),
(557,'You found them.  I trust the elementals from which you removed these bracers were amenable?$B$BHm...death has not only stopped my heart, but robbed me of my comedic timing, it seems.$B$BWell thank you, $N.  You serve the Magus, and hence the Dark Lady, well.',70338),
(567,'You are quite the bounty hunter, $c.  Well done.',70862),
(590,'Incredible! What skill!$B$BThought you\'d be easy prey, $N. Got me good, you did.$B$BHere\'s the coin I promised... not as much as I said it\'d be, but that\'s on a count o\' me lying to ya in the first place.',70862),
(655,'Ah, Gor\'mul you speak of. Yes, from what he says, it seems he has never recovered from the death of Doomhammer.$B$BGor\'mul was a captive here when Thrall and Orgrim fought to free the camp, but as the earth shook and our brethren escaped, he was left behind. He wandered alone and lost for years without direction or hope, until we returned to establish ourselves here in Hammerfall.',70862),
(671,'It will take some time for me to ascertain the true intentions of the Syndicate, but their obvious association with dark, demonic magic troubles me. I will tell you when I know more.',70862),
(672,'Excellent. The spirits of the raptors that gave these eyes will lend strength to the bearer of this amulet.',70862),
(674,'What is this? Polished bone. What use have I for polished bone? Will a trinket restore the Horde to its glory?',70862),
(675,'It did not work, I see. Nonetheless, I feel that showing him the power of the shamans will eventually return Gor\'mul to his once proud self. The amulet\'s power was not great enough to show him our newfound power.',70862),
(677,'The signs of war are upon your garments, and sweat drips from your brow. Good, very good indeed.',70862),
(742,'Welcome to the new frontier, $N.  Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young $c like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle.  Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.$B$BYour presence here tells me that you\'ve come to learn more about the hunt.  Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.',70862),
(744,'Thank you for your help, $N.$B$BMy part in my brother\'s ceremony is almost complete. Giving him his headdress and witnessing the ceremony are all my duty requires of me.',70338),
(747,'The $r of Narache thank you, $N. You show much promise.',70862),
(752,'You traveled all this way just to help an old woman? My my, aren\'t you a keeper? Here, take one of these training manuals with you, so you may learn how to contribute to the community.',70862),
(768,'Ah, these are very nice pieces.  They\'ll make fine leather goods.$B$BHere, $N.  Take this in trade...',70862),
(769,'Ah, good.  Thank you, $N.  My heart swells with pride to see youths interested in the craft of leatherworking.',70790),
(783,'Ah, good.  Another volunteer.  We\'re getting a lot of you these days.$B$BI hope it\'s enough.$B$BThe $r lands are threatened from without, and so many of our forces have been marshaled abroad.  This, in turn, leaves room for corrupt and lawless groups to thrive within our borders.$B$BIt is a many-fronted battle we wage, $N.  Gird yourself for a long campaign.',70790),
(784,'Word of your bravery travels fast, $c. Tales of your victory at Tiragarde Keep will be heralded in Orgrimmar.',70840),
(786,'The Horde would surely prevail if the Kolkar centaurs were to attack. But by preventing such an attack, we have spared our mighty warriors unnecessary bloodshed.$B$BAnd as sure as there is sand in the Tanaris desert, we know that there will be blood spilled before these trying times are through.$B$BYou have served your people well, $c.',70840),
(788,'Hmmm, not bad, $N. But don\'t let it get to your head...you\'ll fight tougher than boars in your career.$B$BNonetheless, you\'ve proven yourself well, and your next trial will be against a considerably more dangerous opponent, so you\'ll need some extra protection.',70840),
(789,'There is an important lesson that you must take away from fighting scorpids. The smallest or largest of opponents can still send you to your doom. In fierce combat, any number of things can prove your downfall.$B$BI have no more to teach you, $N. You have done well, and I will watch your progress with interest.',70840),
(790,'My blow was not enough to kill him, but looking at the damage I inflicted gives me some small measure of pride. That small measure will be all I have to sustain myself if I die, and in that light, the short list of my life\'s accomplishments fills me with anger.',70790),
(791,'Most excellent, $N. Any good $c will surely find a use for this bag on the battlefield.$B$BI salute your vigor and willingness to die in the name of the Horde!',70862),
(792,'You have done well, $N.$B$BAlthough the Vile Familiars were merely pets of the darker powers within the Burning Blade, your success against them foretells greater deeds ahead.',70840),
(794,'You retrieved it!  Well done!$B$BYour efforts within the Burning Blade Coven are key in rooting out this cult in the Valley of Trials.  But I fear they have further aims in our land.$B$BWe have not seen the end of them.',70840),
(804,'From your description of the beast, I believe you must be speaking of Sarkoth! It is no wonder that Hana\'zua was overtaken by it. Aid will be dispatched to him immediately, trouble yourself no more with Hana\'zua\'s plight.$B$BHowever, I must say, I am most impressed to hear that you brought Sarkoth to death. It is a feat to be proud of, $N. And that you would fight for a stranger\'s honor, while other tasks occupied your time, your own honor is heightened.',70840),
(805,'Hm... your report comes at a bad time.  The Burning Blade is not seen here in Sen\'jin, but their evil has taken seed off the coast, on the Echo Isles.$B$BThe orcs are friends of the Darkspear Trolls.  Honorable friends.  We want to help the orcs, but... we need help too.$B',70790),
(806,'Aha!  You got him!$B$BYou do your clan proud, $N.  And because of you, Durotar is free of one more agent of evil.',70862),
(808,'Thank you, $N.  You have saved Minshina.  You have saved my brother\'s spirit from slavery!',70840),
(809,'Neeru wants the Demon Seed destroyed, does he?  Strange...$B$BVery well.  If he wishes the seed gone, then I will tell you how to remove it.',70862),
(812,'$N, you\'ve saved my life. Thank you.$B$BPlease take this; I hope it can at least help you in your travels, if not bring you some coin. From what you say, I won\'t be usin\' it anytime soon. Kor\'ghan is gonna march me through more of his rituals until I prove myself. More killin\' boars, more gatherin\' scorpid tails... <sigh>',70790),
(813,'Here is the antidote, $N. Take it to Rhinag as soon as you can, and be cautious.',70790),
(815,'You might be weak, but at least you\'re not clumsy, $N.$B$BHere, take this and get outta my way. I\'ve got cooking to do.',70840),
(816,'Oh, my son... my beautiful son.$B$BUncertain of my son\'s fate, I have tormented myself since he left. Now that I know what\'s happened, perhaps I can finally begin to mourn.$B$BThank you, $N. Please take this. I was going to give it to Kron as a gift when he returned successful. Now that I know he is dead, I cannot bear to look at it.',70862),
(817,'I am pleased, $N. Because of your help, our people will be protected, and not go cold as the seasons change.$B$BThank you.',70790),
(818,'Well done, young one... well done indeed.',70790),
(819,'Well, I\'ll be...$B$BThis was one of Chen Stormstout\'s kegs. He traveled with Rexxar a long time ago. I haven\'t seen or heard about him in a kodo\'s age. I appreciate you bringing this to me, $N.',70862),
(821,'Haha... I never thought I\'d make more of this stuff ever again.$B$BYou\'ve stirred in me a great sense of nostalgia, $N. Kind of reminds me of the last time I made a batch of trogg brew. Thank you. The memories warm my stomach.',70862),
(822,'Haha! I knew you couldn\'t resist some of this brew. Come back again anytime you want some more, $N. Just bring me more of the ingredients I had you collect.',70862),
(823,'Yes?  You have something to report?  Well then, let\'s have it!',70840),
(824,'This globe... it is most disturbing.  Many of the more powerful elementals receive their power and energy through such devices.  To find one like this nearly intact is one thing - to find it so tainted is another.$B$BI will see that this globe is studied properly by the Earthen Ring.  Perhaps we can bring an end to this corruption of the elements.  Please - accept this as a fair exchange for bringing this globe to the attention of the Earthen Ring.',70862),
(825,'Your recovery mission was a success, $c. I will see to it that these tools get to Orgrimmar with the next caravan.$B$BNicely done.',70862),
(826,'With Zalazane gone, our tribe can again sleep in peace.$B$BThank you, $N.  The Darkspear tribe owes you much.  If you suffer from an ailment, visit my assistant Bom\'bay, behind me.  His voodoo is strong...',70840),
(827,'Good.  Hiding within these collars is the secret behind the Burning Blade.  And I will uncover that secret...',70862),
(828,'Welcome, $N.  Word reached me of your coming, and of your exploits in Durotar.$B$BYou are a $c of growing skill and renown.$B$BStay on the pure path, and your future will be great indeed.',70862),
(829,'Ah, and where did you get this?  Good Margoz in Razor Hill sent you to me, did he?$B$BWell, let me take a closer look...',70862),
(830,'This does not bode well at all. You were wise to bring this information to my attention.',70840),
(831,'Countless times I urged the Warchief not to trust the humans, but personal pride is not what is at stake here.$B$BYou have served the Horde honorably, young $c.$B$BNow excuse me, I must counsel Thrall on these matters at once....',70862),
(832,'<Examines the Eye of Burning Shadow.>$B$BIntriguing.  The voice you heard mentioned my name?  I am known for hunting down enemies of our Warchief, but...it is strange that I was singled out.  Stranger still that the Burning Blade cultists from whom you recovered this pendant have a name so close to my own.$B$BI must study this pendant.  I must study and, and must ponder the meaning of its message.$B$BThank you for bringing this to my attention, $N.  You have done your people a great service.',70790),
(834,'Hey, now isn\'t that just the thing! You\'ve got our supplies back for us. That\'s great. I\'ll be able to get back to work just as soon as I can find someone to haul these sacks for me.',70862),
(835,'I think I can breathe easy now, knowing that the harpies won\'t be bothering our supply caravans anymore. And not one moment too soon, either. I hear I\'m being sent some fun little toys with the next shipment!$B$BYou\'re pretty good at what you do, $N, you ought to track down my boss in Ratchet. I\'ll bet he could find some work for you.$B$BOh, and don\'t worry, I wouldn\'t forget to pay you for the service you provided me.',70862),
(837,'I will pass along word that the quilboars have been removed from their lairs, and that their structures may be set to fire. The removal of the Razormane from Durotar brings us closer to fully securing the borders of our new homeland.',70862),
(840,'Oh, so Takrin sent you? He\'s an excellent scout, I\'m not sure what I\'d do without him.$B$BI\'ll sign your recruitment letter, but what we really need is someone at the Crossroads.',70862),
(842,'Alright, $N. You want to earn your keep with the Horde? Well there\'s plenty to do here, so listen close and do what you\'re told.$B$B I\'m happy to have met you. Thrall will be glad to know that more females like you and I are taking the initiative to push forward in the Barrens.',70862),
(843,'Khazgorm met the fate he earned. I feel no remorse for the fool. He was an infidel on these lands.$B$BMay his death serve as a warning to all those who threaten to disrupt our way of life.$B$BNow let me take a moment to study the dwarf\'s journal....',70862),
(844,'Very good, $N.  With the plainstriders gone we\'ll have an easier time keeping our supply chains intact.  And I hope you learned a few tricks out there in the Barrens, for your next prey has a little more fire in its blood than the plainstriders...',70862),
(845,'Not bad, $N.  Those zhevra hold a lot of strength in their legs.  A sharp kick from them can knock even a tauren on its haunches!$B$BIt looks like you have some strength in you too.  Are you ready for a real challenge?',70862),
(846,'I see you are quite industrious, $c.$B$BNo doubt we shall soon have a fitting surprise for those dwarves.',70862),
(848,'Ah, yes.  These are good specimens.  Potent.$B$BI am Forsaken, and we honor our contracts.  Here is your reward, $N.',70862),
(849,'You have done well, $N! May you be revered in Thunder Bluff as a defender of sacred tauren lands and a champion of the lost tribe.',70862),
(850,'Well done, $N.  The centaur are low, brutish creatures, but a few have the wit and vision to lead.  And those are the most dangerous.$B$BBarak was such a centaur.  It is good that he is dead.',70862),
(851,'Very good.  You must have really stirred up those centaur -- our guards spotted activity down near the Stagnant Oasis, which was probably you.$B$BYou should be proud of your deed, $N.  There is much bravery in you.',70862),
(852,'I commend you, $N.  These centaur are undisciplined and cannot focus their rage as the orcs can, but they are fierce nonetheless.  In defeating them, your valor is proven.',70862),
(853,'Ah, the spores from the Barrens that Helbrim was gathering.  He garnered your aid in delivering them?  Good.$B$BAnd the emulsion is still potent, so you must have wasted no time in the delivery.  Well done, $c.',70862),
(855,'Nicely done.  I\'m sure you\'ve struck fear into the surviving centaurs, $N.  If they have sense, they\'ll now calm themselves and stop their advances.$B$BBut I don\'t think they will, and that is unfortunate.$B$BUnfortunate...for them.',70862),
(857,'At last, the power is mine again! Mine I say!',70862),
(858,'Yep, this looks like the right key. Let me just make sure I know how to work this thing...$B$BHmm... rotation control... This regulates speed and stability... fine arm movement control. Just look at this! I can\'t believe the Venture Company could design something this much better than ours. I\'ve got to get this back to Ratchet!',70862),
(862,'Normally I don\'t like to eat these rodents when they\'re so.... so... ripe. Like to let them rot for a few weeks to really bring out the flavor. But you look so hungry.$B$BLet me fix you some Dig Rat Stew. Ah, there we go.$B$BHere you go!',70862),
(863,'Hopefully we\'ll be able to get something of value from the wrecked shredder prototype... my time\'s running out! I\'ll dispatch a salvage team to Wizzlecrank\'s location on the double.$B$BOh, let me give you something for your trouble, too.',70862),
(865,'Great, you got them!  Now I just need to ground them down and mix them with some wine, and...',70862),
(866,'Yes yes, these are very nice!  I will grow specimens from these roots and study them.  I hope to find new properties from them.  Hidden, valuable properties...!$B$BAnd don\'t worry -- if I do then you\'ll be the first to know.  Because I\'ll need someone to gather more!',70862),
(867,'Oh, these are nice. Real nice... Good job, $N. I look forward to seeing more of your work in the future.',70862),
(868,'You please me, $N. The eggs and the tool. Well done.$B$BAnd for your reward...',70862),
(869,'You got rid of the raptors!$B$BThank you, $N.  You are a $c of worth.',70862),
(870,'You found a fissure in the earth, with gases bubbling from it?  Strange.  This may be an answer to our questions, but we cannot yet be sure.$B$BBut it is a clue.  And I am grateful that you found it.',70862),
(871,'You have done well, $N. Those insolent quilboars will finally learn that the might of the Horde is not to be ignored.',70862),
(872,'Well done, $N. With Kreenig\'s death, there will be a definite decline in the attacks on our caravans.$B$BYour people should be proud to count you among them.',70862),
(873,'You now are one with Isha Awak, $N.  His spirit is with you.  He lurks in your eyes...$B$BEyes that, one day, will learn to see.',70790),
(874,'My brother sent you, did he?  Then you must have proven yourself to him.  If you have earned the respect of Jorn, then you have my respect as well.$B$BAre you ready to tread farther down the hunter\'s path?',70790),
(875,'Excellent work my friend. I think you\'ll go far within the Horde.',70862),
(876,'HA! Well done, $N! Very well done... I wasn\'t sure you were up to the task, but you\'ve proved yourself quite the cut-throat. Thank you again for helping us suppress the Harpy epidemic. Here is your reward, use it well.',70338),
(877,'Your findings are amazing!  The seeds I gave you were dried, and dead.  Whatever rests under these oases can create life from nothing!$B$BWe must study this more...',70862),
(878,'Yes, yes... filled with joy because finally <snort> the Bristleback know my tribe\'s pain, $r. That is how I should feel, but that <snort> is not the case.$B$BYou aid your people and they honor you. Mangletooth aids his people, and what do they do? They turn their backs on him. They forget him and leave him to rot in cage!$B$BI aid them even from locked behind bars and they send no one to save me!',70862),
(879,'It is done then. Better it ends this way, says Mangletooth. <snort> They should have <snort> made sure I was dead when they turned their backs on me instead of leaving <snort> me here in this forsaken cage.$B$BThere is but one task left for you to finish, $r.',70862),
(880,'Thank you, $N.  Studying the beasts of an area can tell much about the area itself.  We shall see what tale these shells tell.$B$BPlease accept my gratitude for your aid ... and perhaps you can use these coins.  I find that I do not need them.',70862),
(881,'You\'ve beaten Echeyakee, and though his days of hunting are over... his spirit is with you.  He will show you the strength found in subtlety, and the honor in mercy.$B$BYour path is still long, $c.  Let\'s hope you stride it well.',70862),
(882,'This fang is merely a token, but what it represents is profound.$B$BIshamuhale\'s strength is in you, $N.  May you use it with temperance.  That is your burden.$B$BThat is your honor.',70790),
(883,'Lakota\'mani is called "Earthshaker" in our language, and his steps are like gathered thunder.  He is with you now, and his courage mingles with yours.  Together there is no conflict you cannot face.$B$BWalk tall, $N.  Walk tall, Earthshaker.',70862),
(884,'The thunder lizard Owatanka is called "Bluebolt" by the tauren, for within him resides a speed that belies his size.  It is said that lightning struck Bluebolt long ago and, fed from the sky\'s rage, the great beast\'s energy is without limit.$B$BMay his energy flow through you, $N.  For you now keep pace with Owatanka.',70862),
(885,'The thunderhawk is a rare beast of the Barrens, and its death can portend great fortune, or great doom.$B$BBut Washte Pawne, called "Spirit Biter" in Taurahe, can bring neither... or both.$B$BThe pain you felt from hunting Spirit Biter is the pang all feel who make great gains at great costs.  The sting you felt is the pain of regret.$B$BBut I can see you have conquered this.  You have learned that regret turns to wisdom, and that through pain one gains strength.$B$BYou have learned much, $N.',70862),
(886,'My brethren in Thunder Bluff were wise to send you, young $c.  For the mystery of the Barrens is one that I alone cannot unravel.$B$BWith your aid, let us hope we can find answers to our questions.',70790);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(887,'You did good, kid. A little more work like that, and it\'ll be one less thing I\'ll have to worry about. Hopefully they\'ll be convinced that they should relocate their operation elsewhere.$B$BIn the meantime, there is the small matter of getting back the goods they stole from me!',70862),
(888,'It\'s a relief to get all this stuff back, so thanks for your help, $N. You know, I could use a $r like you to help out with my operation here. If you\'re ever looking for work, don\'t forget about how well Gazlowe pays for service!',70862),
(889,'Good. Go with Agamaggan\'s spirit as your guide, $r. Return to me if you desire more of Agamaggan\'s magics.',70862),
(890,'Ah, Gazlowe sent you, did he? Just a moment, let me take a look here and check my own logs and make sure I didn\'t have Gazlowe\'s shipment sent to the wrong place.$B$BBet he\'s waiting for those boots from Drizzlek...',70862),
(891,'Alas, the righteous Alliance guns have been silenced. You shall be rewarded for your aid, $N.$B$BNow to tend to the grim task of recovering the bodies of the dead....',70862),
(892,'No dice, eh? I guess it must have been the Freebooters then... Dizzywig\'s on the level, I\'m sure he wouldn\'t cheat me like that. After all, he is on the payroll.$B$BLooks like I\'ve got some goods to get back, $N. What do you say?',70862),
(893,'Excellent, excellent specimens indeed.$B$BThe quilboar are further along than I had expected.$B$BHere, $c, take this and get out of my way. I\'d better take a closer look at these weapons. We may have underestimated our enemy, and that\'s the kind of mistake we can\'t afford to make.',70862),
(894,'A variety of buttons, levers and blinking lights are somewhat erratically arrayed on the face of the control console. A small gauge indicates that the apparatus is currently operating within optimal levels, and indicates that control valves one through three are currently open. There is a small keyhole set into the lower right side of the control panel.',70862),
(895,'Ahhhh! That sort of business. You know, I saw the Heedless once on the open seas. Fearsome ship, or was that boat... those sailors are so particular!$B$BAnyways, watching her glide across the water was quite a sight to see. I\'m glad her infamous captain will trouble my ships no longer.',70862),
(896,'Look at the size of that thing, $N! We\'re going to be rich! Let\'s see, according to the rates I\'ve seen on gems going into Undermine, I should be able to figure out your cut--fifty percent, don\'t worry!$B$BNow let\'s see... I think this should do about right. Pleasure doing business with you, $N.',70862),
(898,'And to think, we thought Firebough was long dead!$B$BYour heroics have earned you a place of honor with the Thalo\'dan Privateers, $N.',70790),
(899,'$C, you take my task seriously, and for that I thank you.$B$BAlthough my desire for revenge remains, I can at least smile seeing that the quilboars have felt pain themselves.',70862),
(900,'The lights indicating the three control valves dim as they are shut off. Green lights slowly fade into yellow, and the switch controlling the apparatus is now moveable, with the valves closed, it can be turned off.',70862),
(901,'Turning the key in the lock, the control console unlocks. A red light at the top of the console turns off and all power drains from the terminal.',70862),
(902,'This is... er... interesting... yes. I\'ll have it sent along to the Tinkers\' Union headquarters in Undermine. I\'m sure after some careful dissection and research, they\'ll be able to make some sense of it.$B$BBut, perhaps I\'ll have a little look myself first...',70862),
(903,'Ah, I see you\'ve been busy, lurking in the grasses and hunting prowlers.  Do you think, then, it is time to face a champion among them?',70862),
(905,'So you\'ve been to the nests and placed the feathers of your prey within them.  That took a fair portion of courage, no doubt about it.$B$BDo you feel a little tougher, $N?  Because you look tougher now then when you first came here.  I guess the Barrens is doing its job.',70862),
(906,'You found the Razormane leader and killed him yourself, $N? Amazing.$B$BI am without words, but that does not mean I am without thanks. The people of the Crossroads would do well to respect your strength.$B$BI must admit, I thought the leader of these raids on our supply lines was another quilboar. Thank you again, $N.',70862),
(907,'It is good to see you return with proof of victory.  And it is good to know you have done so with your bones unbroken.',70790),
(913,'You, like the thunderhawk, should be proud.  You have bested every foe we set you before, and have done so with strength, courage and honor.$B$BBut your path, $N, continues.  In fact, you will find that true hunters forever strive, forever walk their path with the same pride you have shown me.$B$BNow, it is time to move on.',70790),
(914,'You have done it, $N.  You killed the leaders of the Druids of the Fang.  My dreams are now free of their wicked faces, and you have helped save the Barrens from a cursed future.$B$BI thank you, $N.  I thank you for myself, for the druids of Thunder Bluff, and for the land.',70790),
(916,'Thank you, $N.  When I return to Darnassus I will compare the venom within these sacs with the venom of other spiders.  It is my belief that it will have properties linked to the recent growth of our new world tree.',70790),
(917,'Ah, very good.  I will have this egg and the venom transported to Darnassus, then return there when my studies are done here.  I expect to find out a great deal from these specimens, $N.  You have been a great help to me.',70790),
(918,'You got them.  This is good!$B$BI will plant these seeds in special soil I have prepared.  I believe the seeds will sprout into timberlings who are much more docile.  Perhaps later you can see the results!',70790),
(919,'That\'s a lot!  I\'m afraid they\'re spreading at a dangerous rate.  I hope I can solve the riddle of what is tainting them.$B$BThank you for your help, $N.  The land is a cleaner place from your efforts.',70790),
(920,'Ah, $N. I was hoping you\'d be prompt in answering my summons. I have an important task that I would like you to perform.',70790),
(921,'So you have heard the first part of the aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal. There is much more to be told and the task you have begun here will continue through the rest of your journey through Teldrassil and into Darnassus.',70790),
(922,'Ah, a timberling seed?  I wanted to try growing one of these to help Denalan with his studies.$B$BBut I\'m afraid I\'ve discovered that a corruption has grown in many of the timberlings, and seeds from such creatures carry their parent\'s taint.  They are beyond my talents to repair.$B$BDenalan is very skilled with things that grow.  He may find a cure for future timberlings.  He may be their only hope.',70790),
(924,'Your task is complete.  You have destroyed the Demon Seed as Neeru bid.  But this is not the end...$B$BThe destruction of the Demon Seed sent waves of power through the ether, waves of staggering force.  I felt them, and I am sure other beings did as well.  Others who will wonder why their toy was broken...$B$BBut regardless of future troubles, I have something for you.  Neeru sent it as payment.  And he bid me thank you.$B$BSo, thank you.',70862),
(926,'These stones are infused with magical energy, but purposefully flawed.  They are very unstable and once removed from the table they will consume themselves quickly.',70862),
(928,'Ah, I see. You were sent by Tenaron. Well then, it would seem we have much to talk about, much to do, and little time to do it in.$B$BI think we\'d best get started.',70790),
(929,'After the Battle of Mount Hyjal, we were without direction. Nordrassil smoked from the fire it unleashed, and our immortality--the very essence of our beings!--was lost.$B$BIt was in this trying time that the Betrayer was freed from his prison, and Shan\'do Stormrage disappeared. A dark time for all.',70790),
(933,'Shan\'do Stormrage never returned, and the druids were in disarray, and to this day we still do not know what became of him. With Malfurion missing, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm took over the leadership of the druids, convincing the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore that it was time for our people to rebuild, and that it was time for our people to regain their immortality.$B$BWith the approval of the Circle, Staghelm and the most powerful druids grew Teldrassil, the new World Tree.',70790),
(935,'Ah yes, the water I had requested. Tenaron and Corithras certainly took their time in having it delivered... perhaps not choosing the most reliable of messengers... hmm.$B$BNonetheless, I can finally get back to my work then. The weight of Teldrassil\'s problems fall upon my shoulders. A yoke I would wish to soon be rid of.$B$BTake this, you may find some use for it.',70790),
(937,'Thank you for your aid so far--it has been of great relief. Let me inspect these belts to see if we can glean any insights as to the harpy aggression.',70790),
(954,'Ahh... To what could I possibly owe the exceedingly special honor of a $r such as yourself as company. Truly it says much of my current companions--with no offense to my hosts, the noble grells and satyrs--that your presence could be considered an improvement.$B$BBut please, do not let my uncivil tongue drive you from the place. It has indeed been many years, decades even, since I had civil accompaniment.',70790),
(955,'Indeed... The grells of Bashal\'Aran do not possess that which I am searching... however they have come into contact with it recently. Recently... I would reckon that by your time, not mine. Recent for me stretches into the veil of the past, almost another Age...',70790),
(959,'Superb! And just as I was about to lose my job too! I will see to it that Gazlowe gets this gift immediately.$B$BThank you, $N. Nicely done, I say!',70862),
(962,'Ah, splendid specimens. You have done well, $N.',70790),
(972,'Take the water sapta and find the corrupted pool of water in Silverpine, $N. I have great faith in your abilities.',70862),
(983,'As you place the Crawler Legs inside the machine, you hear gears begin to grind. Judging from the banging sounds coming from the Buzzbox, you believe the Crawler Legs are being put in their proper place. Soon the machine begins to hum, and you hear a tiny voice calling out from within.$B$B"Hello? Uhh... Hello! You fixed it! This is Wizbang by the way! Thanks a lot... Hey, you wouldn\'t want to fix another one, would ya?"',70790),
(997,'Ah, it\'s here!  I have waited for this rare earth for quite some time.  I hope it\'s still fresh...$B$BThank you for bringing it to me, $N.  You are a $r who is generous with his time.',70790),
(1013,'Very good.  This book will add nicely to my collections of the workings of Ur.  His knowledge was great, but his conscience held him from true power.  And so when the Scourge came and his strength was tested, it failed.$B$BWe of the Forsaken cannot afford such weakness, if we are to survive...$B$B...If we are to conquer.',70862),
(1014,'Silverpine Forest is finally free from the vice of that wretch Arugal. You have done the Dark Lady a great service, $N. Your tenacity shall be rewarded.',70862),
(1060,'Ahh, a letter from Darsok. I have not heard from him in many years.$B$BSo the last of the Bloodfeathers are dead, eh? That is good news, I can remember when my friend Rokhan went with that crazy mok\'nathal to kill her older sister. Ah, to be young again, like you.',70334),
(1061,'Ah, a $c.  Very good.  We will need your skills to deal with these plunderers!',70862),
(1062,'Bravely done, $N.$B$BWe may ultimately need the wisdom of tauren elders to calm the spirits of Stonetalon, but...$B$BRidding the Venture Company of its personnel is a good first move against them.',70862),
(1063,'I bid you greetings.  You are here seeking counsel?',70338),
(1064,'Magatha sent word of your coming, $N.  Although my heart beats no longer, I still feel sorrow for the spirits of Stonetalon.$B$BThe Forsaken are eager to offer what help we can.',70338),
(1069,'You got them!  Thank you!$B$BI\'ll have these sent to Dizzywig and get them shipped to Booty Bay.  I can already taste the profits!$B$BHere is your cut, $N.  I couldn\'t have made this deal without you.',70338),
(1087,'Already I can feel it... yes... power so sweet... the rushing flood. The kaldorei are foolish to spurn the gifts of this world, to reject the coursing of magic as it flows singing through your veins.$B$BWhat a pale mockery life is without its burning embrace!',70862),
(1088,'I knew Ordanus once, long ago. He had the arrogance of his kind, holding himself above even the Highborne.$B$BHis head does not rise so high now, does it, $N?$B$BI promised you a reward, and you shall have it. Attend to me.',70338),
(1090,'Thanks, $N. It was looking a little dicey there for a second and we\'ve probably drawn far too much attention to ourselves.$B$BThe important part is that we have the ore sample, though, and we should get it to Ziz as soon as possible.',70291),
(1092,'Ahhh, I knew that I did the right thing by telling Piznik to stay behind. I\'m sure the engineers in Undermine will be most interested to look at this...$B$BOf course I\'ll want to keep a little piece for myself, but what they don\'t know won\'t hurt them, yes?',70291),
(1093,'Hey, is that what I think it is? Great!$B$BNow, let\'s see. Ugh... how am I supposed to understand this stuff... can\'t figure out the way gnomes think. Lemme tell you, I\'m surprised they could build the wheel, let alone those flying machines they like so much.',70338),
(1094,'Fizziks, eh? Can\'t say I trust him, but this information seems good enough. What I wouldn\'t give to have the Venture Company out of my hair.$B$BThey do come up with some good machines though... I can\'t deny that we\'ve benefited from using some of the improvements they\'ve devised.',70338),
(1097,'You\'re here to help with my delivery?  Very good!',70862),
(1098,'Vincent\'s body lies broken, and still.$B$BAlthough Deathstalker Adamant will send his report to Hadrec... whatever additional details Vincent gained must remain with him.$B$BBut clutched in his hand is a small trinket...',70862),
(1102,'I see the nasty tribe of Razorfen Kraul now knows the pain of my people. Serves the foul beasts right.$B$BTo drive one from a holy land is a sin worthy of the most severe revenge.$B$BThank you, $N, for aiding me in my plight.',70862),
(1109,'Splendid! This is just the start we needed, $N.',70862),
(1111,'Oh yes.  Parts for Kravel.  I\'m glad you\'re here.  These things have been sitting out here for days, and I was afraid they\'d rust!',70862),
(1130,'So, $N, you have come.  Now, are you prepared to journey through distant lands?$B$BIf so, young $c, then listen on...',70840),
(1131,'In defeating the creature Steelsnap, you have cleansed the Thousand Needles of a horrible taint.$B$BAnd that, $N, is your lesson this day.',70862),
(1144,'Thanks again, friend! I told you I\'d make it worth your while.',70862),
(1145,'Ah, a note from Korran. He has been a loyal servant for some time now. I was wondering how his duties were going in the Crossroads.',70862),
(1149,'It is not until faced with unforeseen adversity that we begin to see how strong our spirits are. You took the leap of faith even though you had no guarantees that you would survive. Your mind is open, and your spirit is prepared for what is to come.$B$BIf you are willing, then the next of your tests is ready.',70862),
(1150,'Grenka was powerful, even by $r standards. You should be proud of your accomplishment this day.$B$BDuring your test of faith you displayed strength of spirit, and now you have shown endurance in battle by taking on the Roguefeather harpies, but the time has come for a new test.',70862),
(1151,'The Test of Strength is done. You have shown strength and bravery, and you are now prepared for the final test before these rites are completed.',70862),
(1195,'Very good. This should fill Rau\'s request just fine. Could you deliver this to him? You might enjoy spending some time out in the Needles.',70862),
(1196,'Hm, yes, this phial of water will serve our purposes perfectly. Because of the shared ancestry of the dryads and the centaurs, the water of the moonwells will enable us to breach the protection of the eternal flame surrounding the centaur relic.',70862),
(1197,'I sense a strange energy emanating from the Hoof... I have no doubt that we will discover surprising new information about the centaur from its study.$B$BMy thanks, $N. Now I must begin to decipher the mysteries you have brought to me.',70862),
(1339,'That\'s right.  I have a task that I can\'t do while I\'m guarding.  In fact, it\'ll take you far from Loch Modan.$B$BYour perfect chance for adventure!',70338),
(1358,'Ah, very good.  If initial reports are true, then the toxicity of these hearts could lead to further advances in our knowledge of poisons.$B$BThis is a welcome delivery, $N.  Your reward is well earned.',70790),
(1359,'Ah yes, the heart samples of which Renferrel spoke.  I am eager to experiment with these... it is always of interest to the Royal Apothecary Society when new forms of toxins are discovered.',70790),
(1464,'May fire burn within your heart, $N.$B$BThe elements await you.',70790),
(1470,'Though you are still untested and young in your learning, you have proven that you possess sufficient ability to master the summoning and binding of an imp. Do not be deceived by an imp\'s size. Though it lacks physical strength, it possesses powers and a cleverness that will serve you well.$B$BAttend me carefully, $N, for I will not repeat this lesson, and I will leave its mastery to you.',70235),
(1471,'You have done well, $N. Now, I will impart to you the spell used for summoning the voidwalker.$B$BThe power that it unleashed upon you is now yours to command. Use it wisely.',70245),
(1473,'Ah, this is excellent. Like as not, Perrine was ignorant to the true power of the musty book he had stolen from us.$B$BIt will not fall out of our hands again. Observe, $N, the structure of the spell, the manner in which your power must be channeled.',70235),
(1478,'Good, I see Ageron managed to find you, $N. Let us waste little time with small talk and pleasantries and focus on your training. There is still much you have to learn.',70235),
(1483,'I thought those Venture Company higher-ups were slave drivers, but then I met Sputtervalve, the cruelest of them all!$B$BHa! Though it\'s better than being out of a job, I suppose... Or worse, working with that Gerenzo. If you\'re here to help, I\'ve got something for you to do.',70862),
(1485,'Throughout your training as a $c, you will learn to call forth beings of many sorts. Some may not seem it, but all are useful tools.$B$BDo not be fooled by the imp\'s small size. As you no doubt noticed, it is still a formidable adversary.',70790),
(1486,'Your efforts shall not go unnoticed in gathering these hides, $N.$B$BThank you for your dedication.',70790),
(1487,'As a Disciple of Naralex, I commend your bravery, $N.$B$BYour aid in ridding the caverns is the first step in our long plight to see the Barrens restored.$B$BThank you and may you prosper.',70790),
(1489,'I bid you greetings, $N.  You are welcome here, and I suggest you gather all your strength.  For the task we now set before you ... is a dire one.',70862),
(1490,'Yes, it is true.  I know of the druids in the Wailing Caverns.  I have seen their twisted, scaled faces.  I know their crimes, and I know their plans.$B$BYou must stop them, $N.',70862),
(1491,'Great, you got it!  I can\'t wait to try it out.  This is going to make me a fortune, I just know it!$B$BThank you, $N.  Take this, and after I\'m rich I\'ll send you more, I promise!',70790),
(1492,'A small enough crate. Yes, I should be able to find room for this aboard the ship. It sails with the next tide, I trust this is soon enough? Excellent. Let me just enter it into my ledger.$B$BAll taken care of! Good day to you, $c.',70862),
(1498,'Ah.  I see you have defeated the thunder lizards, which proves you are tough.  Now I will show you how tough skin and shrewd movements can combine to form an impenetrable wall of defense.$B$BLearn your lesson well, $N.  And be ready for future instruction.',70338),
(1499,'You have done well, $N.$B$BAlthough the vile familiars were merely pets of the darker powers within the Burning Blade, your success against them foretells greater deeds ahead.',70790),
(1501,'Good. I hope you inflicted some other losses on the Burning Blade when you went to retrieve this.$B$BThey have been a source of great annoyance for the Warchief, and a great blight upon warlocks as a whole.',70862),
(1504,'You have done well, $N. I will show you how to summon the voidwalker similar to the one you just defeated.$B$BYou should know that we have high expectations for you, and you have, so far, matched them.$B$BDo not let it go to your head, however, as the tasks that still lie before you will make this seem as simple as waking in the morning.',70862),
(1505,'Hello, young one.  Here for some instruction, are you?',70338),
(1506,'Good. I was afraid Ophek wouldn\'t reach you.$B$BIt is time that I further your $c training. Any business you have currently will have to wait.$B$BI trust there will not be a problem with this?',70862),
(1516,'Excellent. Your success shows that you are prepared.$B$BOf all the elements, earth represents the foundation of all things. It is your strength, your stamina, and your patience. Earth will protect you, but only if shown the proper respect. Like the other elements, even earth can be fickle. Earth is the basis for life, and by observing its laws, you will gain greater wisdom. Never forget the secrets earth shares with you.$B$BI shall make a sapta for you now, and by accepting it, you will realize your path.',70790),
(1517,'Ah... $N... pleased is the earth to have you here.$B$BBound together in body and spirit, you will go forward knowing that the mountains are your strength; the plains, your patience; and the world itself your essence.$B$BStanding before the earth humbly is all that is required of you for you to pass this rite. But the others are not as passive. They may be chaotic and often violent, but such is the nature of the elements. Dual natures opposing one another, you must come to learn these things intricately.',70790),
(1518,'Excellent!$B$BThe totem I will craft for you is more than a symbol of your status among $c--it has abilities beyond that. One use of the totem is as a focus for spells. Those spells are tied to the earth, and as you earn greater and greater wisdom, more of the earth\'s abilities will be made accessible to you.$B$BThe trainers will know when you are ready for greater knowledge.$B$BBut for now, take this earth totem...',70790),
(1524,'Ah, my mistake, $N. I apologize. I did not realize you possessed the Torch. I am pleased to make your acquaintance.$B$BMany adventurers find their way here while looking for lost treasure or the promise of mystical creatures to slay, only to be turned away from a seemingly empty shrine. But we know the truth, do we not, $N?$B$BThis shrine holds a greater secret from the mundane members of the Horde. To us, it is sacred.',70790),
(1525,'These will do nicely, $N.$B$BFire is more than chaos and destruction--do well to remember that. It is also about life, and creation. All things are tied together in such a way. Forces oppose one another, but at the same time, one cannot exist without the other. Both extinguish one another, but also give one another meaning. Always remember this.$B$BUsing different types of magic in conjunction with one another will show not only true skill, but great wisdom.',70790),
(1526,'A white hot flame ignites within the bowl as you place the ember within. You can feel the magical effects of the sapta coursing through your body and the fire dances rhythmically before you.$B$BYou place the top of the torch within the basin, and it immediately catches on fire.',70790),
(1527,'Your spirit burns brighter than any torch I\'ve ever seen, $N, and for that, you should be proud.$B$BIf you continue down this path, the elements will be yours to command, and our brethren will look to you for guidance and wisdom. Let me be the first to congratulate you and present to you your newest totem.',70790);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(1529,'The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.$B$BYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.',70790),
(1530,'Yes?$B$BMmm, I have a feeling I know what you\'re going to ask me: what would possess someone to live out here in the deepest part of the Barrens, the threat of quilboar all around, and no protection? Well, we all have our reasons to justify why we act the way we do. The real question is, what brings a lowly $r to the deepest reaches of the Barrens to speak to a woman who obviously has no concern for her own well-being?$B$BI\'m willing to bet we both know the answer to that.',70862),
(1534,'Wonderful, $N. With all three samples gathered, I can create for you a vial of the purest water any living creature will find. It will be used in the next steps of your rite of passage.$B$BI am pleased to count you among our kind, $N. You do all $c proud, and I look forward to hearing about your exploits in the future.',70862),
(1535,'I thought some bloodshed might ensue if you tried to take water from the pool. It is a pity the quilboar do not realize that all living things are tied together; that their greed only perpetuates the pain and suffering of their people. How much could they accomplish if they were to put their differences aside and their clans came together.$B$BAgain, a pity, but more than likely a boon for the other races of the Barrens.',70862),
(1536,'This is good, $N. You\'re dedicated to the task at hand and have the ability to seek out that which is needed.$B$BOne more sample is all I need to create the reagent needed for your sapta. Islen will be pleased as well.',70862),
(1881,'Greetings, $N.  You were wise to answer my call, and wiser still if you heed what I next say...',70862),
(1882,'Ah, a fine specimen this is.  I will send it to be studied by our apothecaries to determine the extent of the Plagueland\'s taint.$B$BWell done, $N.  For your services, I present to you this choice: an orb or staff.  Whichever you choose, you will find it quite useful.',70790),
(1918,'You find a nasty ball of water and decide to bring it to me?  Who am I, the Earthen Ring or something?$B$BActually, that does give me an idea... perhaps you do need the Earthen Ring for this.  I mean, if it helps clear up the situation at the lake for good, then I\'m all for it.$B$BYou know who the Earthen Ring are, $N?',70862),
(1944,'Ah, very good.  I trust the satyrs of Xavian gave you little trouble?$B$BThank you, $N.  I will study this sample of Xavian water immediately. ',70862),
(1960,'Very good, $N.  The creatures within these containment coffers will be studied by our finest minds, and the reason behind their presence in the Undercity will be determined.$B$BIf their appearance is caused by a rift in the natural flow of magic, then we must determine if the rift was random.  If it was not random, but instead an attack by some magical force, then we must prepare for future, more serious disturbances.',70790),
(2038,'You\'ve done the movement a great service, $N. The troggs and leper gnomes infesting Gnomeregan will soon feel the brunt of a gnomish air assault!',70862),
(2039,'So Gnoarn doesn\'t trust my reconnaissance abilities? I wonder why...$B$BNevermind that, I need your assistance! Nay! The movement needs your assistance!',70862),
(2158,'Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold -- that\'s our motto! Please, take a seat by the fire and rest your weary bones.$B$BWould you like to try a sampling of some of our fine food and drink?',70790),
(2159,'Ah yes, the delivery of herbs from Shadowglen.  It is a shame Porthannius could not bring it himself, for we have much to discuss, he and I.  But I am glad to get the herbs nonetheless, and I am glad you came.$B$BWhile you are here, please, rest yourself.  Heroes must keep their strength and spirits high, and must find rest and solace whenever they may.  For to neglect one\'s peace of body and mind is a sure path to failure.$B$BSo... rest.',70790),
(2161,'Ah, this is the food Ukor brought to the Valley of Trials.  Did they not need it?  Well, I guess they like to starve you heroes in training.  Builds spirit, they say!$B$BThank you for returning the food.  I\'ll stick it back on the shelves... but here, let me offer you some refreshment first!$B$BAnd don\'t forget to rest here in the inn.  You may be a brave $c ready to take on the world, but if your energy is sapped you won\'t be doing yourself, or the Horde, much good.',70840),
(2519,'So, Sister Aquinne sent you?',70790),
(2841,'I knew you could do it, $N! Sovik on the other hand, he had his doubts.$B$B<Nogg clears his throat.>$B$BNow that we have the blueprints in our possession, it is only a matter of time before we figure out all of the gnomish innovations that went into the creation of the rig and make them goblin innovations for our new shredder models.$B',70862),
(2842,'She\'s a beauty, isn\'t she? Pinnacle of goblin transport technology -- only exploded a dozen or so times.$B$BDon\'t worry, $N, I\'ve got her all fixed up. She won\'t blow up on you - and if she does, it\'ll be quick and painless.',70862),
(2843,'All done! When you\'re ready, just step on the pad.',70862),
(2945,'You place the ring inside the Sparklematic 5200 and deposit a silver coin into the slot.$B$BPainful grinding noises emanate from the machine as it begins to jerk around violently.  One can only guess what is happening with the ring inside the machine...$B$BThe machine suddenly stops, trumpeting its cessation with a simple "Ding!"  The item receptacle opens up to reveal a small box that is neatly wrapped with a red bow.  It would appear that the Sparklematic 5200 also gift wraps!',70862),
(2949,'A ring from Gnomeregan?  Let\'s see... not mine, but interesting.$B$BThe Gnomeregan thing - couldn\'t have happened to a nicer bunch of numbskulls.  For years they\'re a joke, and now almost overnight they\'re making better rigs than us?$B$BDark Iron dwarves had the ring?  That\'s even more interesting!  You know, maybe the gnomes stole their crazy golem plans and modified them.  Those Dark Irons, they\'d definitely want some major payback.  It\'s certainly worth investigating.$B$BYou know, about that ring...',70862),
(2950,'Here\'s your ring, better than before.  Thanks again for the information about those Dark Iron dwarves.  This seems like a reasonable lead as to how those gnomes suddenly were struck with goblin-like inspiration.',70862),
(2953,'The Sparklematic 5200 comes to life, lurching to and fro.  Inside, the helpless grime that has encrusted the object placed within it is being pulverized by the machine\'s gnomish cleaning agent.$B$BThe Sparklematic 5200 comes to a halt, heralded by a familiar "ding!"  The item receptacle of the machine spirals open, revealing a neatly wrapped box.',70862),
(2983,'Hmmm, Swart sent you to me, did he?$B$BWell then, Swart could always be trusted, so that must mean you\'re ready to take part of the next sapta--the sapta of fire.$B$BI see it in your eyes already, the burning, the desire. You\'ve tasted power, and now you\'re ready for more of it. Patience, $N. Remember what earth taught you. Power and destruction will come easily, but you must still know when to stay your hand.',70790),
(3082,'Now we teach them those things, and they teach us others. We become one race... almost. We be allies for long time now. So you remember to help them. And Jen\'shan remember to help you.$B$BJen\'shan teach you da ways of the $c--teach you good. You never forget, $c\'s be respected greatly by da tribe. You be havin\' a large role to play in da future... you never forget that.$B$BWhen you feel da need, come to Jen\'shan. She teach you as much as she can when she feel you ready.',70840),
(3084,'As you probably know, the elements give us our power. Fire, earth, water and air--these are our tools.$B$BOur strength comes from the spirits of our ancestors. We are the leaders of our people. Like Thrall is to the Horde, so shall we be to the villages and towns we visit. They will look to us for wisdom and protection. To be better prepared, you must train often. When you feel you\'ve gained more power, come to me and I shall teach you what I can.',70790),
(3088,'Now that you know where I\'m holding up, I should let you know: the Shattered Hand\'s asked me to look out for you. They want me to train you and keep you informed of anything they might need. Even if you\'re not interested in helping them yet--which you\'d be a fool not to be--I\'ll do what I can to train you... for a small fee. Come back to me anytime you think you\'re ready, and we\'ll see what you\'re ready to learn.',70338),
(3097,'There is only one thing you must know: we have survived through will alone. It is faith in ourselves that separates us from others, and with our powers, we will cause great change in all of Azeroth. The weak will come to lean on you. The lepers will call you Lady. And the ignorant will look to you for guidance. It is my duty to make sure you have the necessary tools so when the time comes, you are prepared. As you grow in experience, seek me out. I will teach you greater powers if you are ready.',70862),
(3098,'You must return to me often if you are to become powerful enough to destroy those who would oppose us. The rules of magic still apply to you, $N. You will still find corruption follows you like hungry wolves in the night. You will find its caress is not unlike an addiction, an old lover still wanting to be by your side. But these things can be staved off. These things will only control you if you allow them to.$B$BGo now, return to me when you\'ve grown more powerful.',70790),
(3099,'I mentioned a slave still being a slave, no matter the master. Do you remember? We both know that it is that type of control--that type of power--that now drives us. We seek to have creatures serve us. We know we are more powerful and deserve more respect than others give us ... and so now we look to take it.$B$BI will be your ally in this struggle--the struggle for our own freedom. Freedom to seek our own allegiances. When you feel ready, return to me and I will teach you all I know.',70235),
(3103,'As you grow in experience, return to me and I will do what I can to impart my knowledge upon you. Until then, go with compassion in your heart, and let wisdom be your guide. Remember, the world only becomes a better place if you make it so.',70790),
(3104,'Haha, I knew my note would not dissuade you from your path. So, you\'re prepared then, are you? Prepared to accept your fate? Prepared to challenge the gods and any other forces that stand before you in the pursuit of knowledge and power?$B$BI will not lie, $N, you will be feared as much as respected. But also know this, I will be here for you when you need training. Simply seek me out as you grow more powerful.',70790),
(3117,'As you experience what Shadowglen has to teach you, come see me--I will be able to help you understand more about your role as a $c and what you are capable of.$B$BThese are dangerous times, $N, do not take for granted the skill of your pets--there are things in this world more dangerous than you can imagine. Go with Elune and return to me again.',70790),
(3221,'Ah, very good.  There is a matter regarding the wolf hearts you brought to me earlier that demands our attention.',70790),
(3261,'Greetings, young one.  You are here to walk the hunter\'s path?$B$BVery good.  Let us begin.',70790),
(3281,'Aha!  So the raptors did hide the silver at their lair.  It\'s hard to believe these beasts would have the desire for silver.  Perhaps the stories of their intelligence are not as far from the mark as I thought!$B$BThank you, $N.  Take this as a reward for your service to us, and know that the guards of the crossroads owe their next month\'s pay to you.',70862),
(3301,'Ah, what is this?  This shell has an inner glow, as if it still pulses with life.  Amazing!  I must study it further.$B$BThank you, $N.  With luck, this shell will hold a secret I can use to aid the poor land of Silverpine.',70862),
(3369,'Falla sent you to me? Well now, let\'s see that shard that you say she was so hesitant to talk about...$B$B<Hamuul peers into the shard>$B$BOh... I didn\'t... Well.$B$B$N, thank you for delivering this to me. It isn\'t wise to speak of things such as this, though, I advise you. These are matters that you should not concern yourself with.$B$BLet\'s just say that things in the Emerald Dream are not as we thought...$B$BPerhaps in the future, our paths may cross again.$B',70790),
(3513,'Well now... Where did you find this?',70862),
(3519,'Oh dear; I was wondering why I hadn\'t seen Iverron yet today. And I\'ve always warned him about those spiders...',70790),
(3521,'Thank Elune that you have gathered these ingredients so quickly!$B$BIn just a moment, I will have the antidote prepared.',70790),
(3522,'What is this, $N?$B$BOh, I knew Dirania would be able to help me!$B$B<Iverron drinks the antidote.>$B$BI\'m always getting into trouble and Dirania, well, she always manages to help me out of it.$B$BI am feeling much better, but I think I will sit here for a while longer, until I feel completely better. Well, that, and I was hoping you\'d clear a path for me through those vicious Webwood spiders...',70790),
(3524,'I hope the murloc did not give you much trouble in collecting this for us!  I will be sure to get this on the next hippogryph to Darnassus.  The Temple of the Moon has given me some funds to hand out for assistance; please have some with our thanks.$B$BYour success here emboldens me to offer you a chance to aid the Temple of the Moon further, if you are interested... ',70790),
(3861,'"BACAW!!!"$B$BThe chicken starts to gobble up the feed you put down.$B$BAfter a moment, the chicken looks around, startled. It uncomfortably shuffles back and forth. Is this chicken pregnant? You think you better check underneath it.',70840),
(3901,'I am finished with you, $N - you have shown yourself to be worthy of the freedom that you have been given.  Many will stand against you for what you have become, but know that no matter what they may try to do against us, we are free and will not be shackled again.$B$BTake these and be on your way.  You have much to accomplish, $c.',70862),
(3902,'Great work $N, I knew you weren\'t useless.  Here - have one of the better items I\'ve found out of the lots that have been collected so far.',70862),
(3903,'Oh, Deputy Willem told you to speak with me?  He\'s a brave man and always willing to help, but his duties keep him stuck at Northshire Abbey and I\'m afraid the problem I have today is beyond him.$B$BPerhaps you can help me?',70790),
(3904,'Oh thank you, $N!  You saved my harvest!  And I hope you showed a few of those Defias that they can\'t cause trouble around here.$B$BWe might be short on guards these days, but we\'re lucky to have heroes like you to protect us!',70790),
(3905,'Let\'s see here...$B$BOh my!  Milly\'s grapes have been saved!  When she told me that brigands overran her vineyards I nearly despaired, but my faith in the Light did not waver!$B$BAnd through your bravery,  we now have grapes for more wine!  May the Light bless you, $N, and keep you safe!',70790),
(3921,'Oh, what\'s this?  A samophlange, you say?  What\'s a samophlange??$B$BAh... but look at the way it moves when you handle it.  And there\'s the sound of intricate gears inside.  Oh my!  I want to fix it and see what it does, don\'t you??',70862),
(3922,'Great, you got them!  Now I can get to work...',70862),
(3923,'What\'s this?  Why, it\'s a samophlange!  Where did you get this thing?  Have you been poking around the Venture Company holdings in the Barrens?$B$BYou must be very brave, or very stupid.',70862),
(3924,'You got the manual!  I can\'t wait to read it and find out how to fix the Samophlange!  I spoke with Sputtervalve in Ratchet--he wanted to thank you for your help, and wanted to reward your efforts.$B$BI want to thank you too, and if I ever get this thing fixed I\'ll let you know...',70338),
(4021,'You have done it!  You have defeated the Kolkar!$B$BI will be sure Thrall receives word of your actions here, $N.$B$BStand tall.  You do yourself, and the Horde, proud.',70840),
(4161,'Always remember what I have shown you today, $N. You are part of the balance that the night elves strive to keep intact, even during troublesome times.',70790),
(4402,'Wonderful, $N! As promised, here is your cactus apple surprise. Pick one of these training manuals, too. I\'ve got plenty to go around.',70840),
(4495,'I\'m so glad you found me, $N. How did you know I was here?',70790),
(4542,'More bad news! These centaurs have gone too far! They raided one of my supply caravans and slaughtered the whole party. This is an outrage, and it will not go unpunished!$B',70862),
(4581,'Ah, Shindrell\'s report!  Many thanks, $N.  Shindrell is a fine sentinel, brave and keen.  I must read this for clues of a wickedness I fear is moving through Ashenvale.',70450),
(4601,'You insert the grime-encrusted item and three silver coins into the Sparklematic 5200.  The machine surges to life in a frenzied attempt to purge the grime from the unknown item.  Loud, violent churning sounds beat from the heart of the machine.  The metal frame of the beast creaks and groans as it lurches from side to side...',70862),
(4603,'The Sparklematic 5200 comes to life, lurching to and fro.  Inside, the helpless grime that has encrusted the object placed within it is being pulverized by the machine\'s gnomish cleaning agent.$B$BThe Sparklematic 5200 comes to a halt, heralded by a familiar "ding!"  The item receptacle of the machine spirals open, revealing a neatly wrapped box.',70862),
(4605,'As quickly as it started, the Sparklematic 5200 comes to an abrupt halt.  A simple "ding" is heard from the machine, and the mouth of the machine spirals upward.  Inside the Sparklematic 5200 is a small box wrapped in a little bow.  The machine would appear to wrap an object up after eliminating its grime-encrusted status.  Even if the machine didn\'t work, at least the item is now wrapped in a pretty box.$B$BWell, there is one way to find out if it cleaned the item or not...',70862),
(4641,'Another one of Kaltunk\'s recruits, hm?$B$BA sorry state of affairs we find ourselves in if this is the best the Horde can produce. No matter. By the time we think you\'re ready to leave the Valley, you\'ll be a proud warrior of the Horde.',70840),
(4821,'Yes, finally... the mysterious egg has finally been delivered to me. Now, let me take a closer look at this... What..! What is this..?$B',70862),
(4841,'For my gratitude, this is for you, $N.',70862),
(4865,'Vengeance! So, the legend of Arikara is true. Indeed, this is a problem that must be resolved immediately.',70862),
(4881,'They come to kill me?  I will show them how a Tauren fights!',70862),
(4921,'I understand. Thank you, $c.',70862),
(4966,'Thank you for your help, $N. I couldn\'t have held them off without you.',70862),
(5041,'Haha! Thank you, $N! This will help us greatly. You\'re a boon to the Crossroads and to the Horde. If there is anything I can do for you, please, let me know.',70862),
(5043,'May your aim be unerring, and the mark of your weapon be true, skyborne.$B$BAgamaggan\'s spirit is with you. Return <snort> to me if you wish. Mangletooth will bless you again if the great boar god deems me worthy. <snort>',70291),
(5044,'Your enemies should fear you even more, $r. <snort>$B$BTell Mangletooth tales of your cunning in battle when next we meet--be it in this life, or the next. <snort>',70790),
(5045,'Our greatest warriors, and our greatest <snort> shamans would envy your will, $r.$B$BDefeat more of the Bristlebacks knowing that they cannot stop you! <snort>',70862),
(5052,'Ah, you do understand. <snort> My words were not lost on your ears, $r. Mangletooth may be caged, but no cage can stop Agamaggan\'s power! <snort>$B$BThe touch of the shard, the feel of it... it has been a long time, $r.$B$BDo you know what it is like? To have your power severed from you?$B$BBut, that is a tale for another time. I promised you information. I promised you Agamaggan\'s power. My people turned their backs on Mangletooth. Now, I lose you upon them. <snort>',70862),
(5062,'Good, you have gathered the essential amount of Incendia agave. This rare herb found only in Thousand Needles will help light the dormant sacred fire of life.$B$B<Magatha begins to enchant the Incendia agave.>',70862),
(5064,'Great Spirit Totem! This is dire news indeed. I must begin to plan for whatever may come.$B$B$N, as promised, here is your reward for your brave service.',70862),
(5088,'This does not make sense. Why would Arikara be after Cairne Bloodhoof? Magatha could not be wrong, she is our most powerful shaman.$B$B<Motega shakes his head.>$B$BRegardless, your great deed to the Horde shall not go unnoticed - please, choose one of these as a reward for your aid.',70862),
(5147,'Hah! Well, this is excellent news! I was starting to think that he would never be brought to justice!$B$BHere you are, $N... and thanks. News of Arnak\'s foul deeds boiled my blood!',70862),
(5151,'My hypercapacitor! This will keep me busy for a while until I can figure out what it does...',70862),
(5261,'That\'s true.  I\'m looking for someone to hunt me some wolves!  Are you that person?',70790),
(5441,'Good, good.  Maybe they\'ll think twice before slacking next time!  Thanks for the help!',70840),
(5481,'What\'s this? Gloom weed?! I\'ve no need for gloom weed! That mindless mass of flesh is out there picking daisies and convincing the Lady knows how many dupes like you into doing the same. No offense.$B$BVery well, you\'re here now and that\'s all that matters. Since I\'m not going to bother to try to explain things to that abomination how about you collect what I really need... doom weed!',70862),
(5482,'Ah, my doom weed. Excellent!$B$B<Junior Apothecary Holland rubs his hands together greedily.>$B$BThese will come in quite handy. You\'ve done me, uh, the Lady, a fine service today, $N. As promised here is the reward that you deserve.',70862),
(5545,'Excellent! Thanks to you, I should be able to complete the order in time. To show my gratitude, I would like to offer some coin as compensation for your troubles.$B$BThank you and farewell.',70790),
(5623,'I\'m glad you\'ve arrived, $N. We have much to discuss about your future and your path within the Light.',70790),
(5624,'Excellent, $N. With one more healthy guard out there to help the town, we\'ll be that much safer. I\'m glad to see you\'re already learning to use your abilities wisely. If you feel you are ready for more training at any time, please come back to me. But for now, take this robe. It will let others know that you are one of our order. If you don\'t want to wear it, that\'s fine. Later there will be more tests and this robe isn\'t necessary for those.',70790),
(5651,'Finally, you\'ve arrived. Your faith alone will not allow you to pass the trials before you, young one. A sense of urgency and some ambition will help too.',70862),
(5722,'The body looks seriously beaten by clubs or fists, but most of the corpse\'s clothing and equipment still looks present. It seems the troggs do not overly care much for material wealth.$B$BYou begin to search the body for anything of interest that might help Magatha.',70862),
(5723,'I am glad to see you took Magatha\'s task seriously. Thank you, $N. I\'m sure the troggs will have a harder time coming to the surface with their numbers so greatly reduced.$B$BPerhaps in the future we can take time to figure out where such creatures came from, and what they really want.',70862),
(5724,'Excellent, $N. Thank you.$B$BMagatha told me that if you were successful in finding her clansman that you be given this. Please, take it in thanks.',70862),
(5725,'Good, $c. You have done well in serving the Dark Lady. Your continued perseverance and ambition will be of great use to the Lady\'s subjects. Return to me again in the future. Perhaps I will have other tasks for you that will aid the Dark Lady in her attempts at overtaking the Lich King and completely freeing the Scourge.',70862),
(5726,'Good, $N! The spirits be praised, perhaps you are the one who will finally put my greatest fears to rest! Who would suspect someone so young and so brave would rise up and champion our cause? You remind me of myself when I was younger. I will ensure that you are justly rewarded for your efforts if we both survive the coming storm.$B$BBut there is time for more praise later. You\'ve not accomplished anything in comparison to what you will face... but this is a good start.',70862),
(5727,'Excellent! Most excellent, $c!$B$BWhat you have done this day is only the first step in a much broader foundation--a foundation that we will build the destruction of the Shadow Council on, once and for all.$B$BTell me all he said... and leave not one word out--it may be more important than you realize.',70862),
(5728,'I am glad you\'ve returned, $N. Some of those loyal to me brought word immediately that the caverns below Orgrimmar were in disarray now that their leaders have been slain. I even heard reports that Neeru was more than agitated. It seems we\'ve put a dent in his armor. I can\'t say I\'m displeased... even with such a minor victory.',70862),
(5729,'What is it?! Oh, you, $c... my apologies. My anger rivals that of a rabid kodo bull... but perhaps it is my own fault. In sending travelers into Ragefire Chasm, I should have seen the possibility that some harm would come from it. It seems both Bazzalan and Jergosh were taken unaware and slain by some of Thrall\'s do-gooders. A most inopportune time, but there is nothing that can be done about it now.',70862),
(5730,'Ashenvale? Hmm, I had not heard of any presence of the Council or the Burning Blade in Ashenvale. My spies will investigate, $N. You have done well.$B$BFor now, rest, and keep yourself occupied with other tasks. I will call upon you again soon.$B$BLok-Tar Ogar!',70862),
(5761,'Ha! You\'ve done it! Thrall will be so pleased.$B$BI will ensure this heart is taken care of properly.$B$BFor now though, you must celebrate your victory. I will inform Thrall of your success.$B$BThank you for your aid, $c.',70862),
(5881,'This is great news; I have been sitting here guarding this hunk of wood for too long. Now I can spend some time with my family... Yippee!',70862),
(6062,'You have done well, $N. I believe you are ready for your next task.',70790),
(6063,'Excellent, $N! You are quite a fast learner.',70790);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(6081,'A young $c, I see. Yes, I will grant you the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.$B$BNow, go, $c. We will speak again, at a later date.$B',70790),
(6082,'You have learned all I can teach you, $N. It is time for you to take what you have learned here and choose a pet of your own.$B$BHere you are, $N. I will now give you the power to tame a beast, as well as call it and dismiss it as you see fit. Use your new skills with pride; you have earned them.$B',70790),
(6083,'You are a swift learner, $N. You have done well.',70790),
(6101,'I see your commitment and that you have understood what I have taught you, $N.',70790),
(6102,'You have learned all I can teach you, $N. May I offer you one more piece of advice: use discretion when choosing your first pet. Will you choose a creature of the land, of the water, or of the sky? Whatever it may be, without doubt, your pet will be with you for quite some time.$B$BHere you are, $N. I will now give you the power to tame a beast, as well as call it and dismiss it as you see fit. Use your new skills with pride; you have earned them.',70790),
(6103,'A fledgling $c, I see. Yes, I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.$B$BRemember, $N, always respect the balance and live in awe of nature around you. Now, go forth. We shall speak again, at a later date.',70790),
(6126,'Greetings young $c, I\'m glad to see you ready and eager to learn about the curing of poisons.$B$BWhile most druids in the past were put through pre-planned trials, your work will involve no such thing.  There has been a rash of animal poisonings at the Crossroads in the Barrens, and they\'re unable to bring it under control.  Someone there has requested Moonglade for aid, so we are sending you there to aid them.  This is no exercise - the work you\'ll do is quite real.  Bear this in mind.',70790),
(6127,'By my ancestors, this water is disgusting!  No wonder the gazelles are sick.$B$BSomething is polluting the water, and in turn beginning to wreck the northern Barrens ecosystem.  Sick gazelles have been sighted all north of the east-west road here.  While this water is most likely a primary source of the sickness spreading, there\'s something else at work here.$B$BThis water, believe it or not, will help us formulate a cure.  While I research this water, I have need of some items to formulate a cure...',70790),
(6128,'This is good, $N, so much so that it should be enough to make some ample doses of the salve - at least enough to start to make a difference.$B$BMaking a cure for poisons can be quite difficult at times because each one often requires a very specific antidote to counteract it.  Imagine being able to cure a poison at will without having to worry about the exact ingredients of what the antidote must be!$B$BNow, let me get to work on this!',70790),
(6129,'You have done well in tending to the sickly gazelles of the Barrens; they are unwitting victims of a greater taint and corruption that is spreading all throughout the land.  You tauren are most eager to understand the ways of Cenarius; you, like your elders in Thunder Bluff, are proving that the need for balance transcends artificial racial barriers.$B$B$N, you\'ve proven your worth as an friend of nature and the Circle - take this as a symbol of such.',70790),
(6130,'Welcome back - I\'ve been following your progress on this lesson since you left, and I must admit I was surprised to learn about the situation at the Crossroads.  This does bear some further investigation, as the introduction of such poisons into the environment is most upsetting to the balance.$B$BYou handled yourself with grace under pressure.  For that, I can find no better way to reward you than with permanent power over poison.  Use it well, $N... use it well.',70790),
(6181,'You have to get this note to Stormwind?  That\'s not a problem, you can take one of my gryphons!',70862),
(6261,'A crate for Westfall, eh?  Have you been to Westfall before?  If so, then it\'s no problem, my friend.  I have plenty of gryphons trained to fly that route!',70862),
(6281,'Ah, a note from Quartermaster Lewis?  I\'m not surprised he needs more gear.  Sentinel Hill is far away, in a land Stormwind has all but forgotten.$B$BWell thank you, $N.  Here\'s some money to cover your travel costs.',70862),
(6282,'This is most excellent news! Tell me again how you cast fear into the cold hearts of those vile harpies. The Bloodfuries have been dealt a serious blow!',70862),
(6283,'Already I feel the anger leave me. What will I do with my time? Knowing evil moves near my land kept my thoughts moving, though now they are silent. Perhaps this is a good thing... maybe now I can focus on the good, as all Tauren should.$B$BPlease accept this as a reward for your troubles.',70862),
(6284,'Good hunting, $N! Besseleth is an old predator in these parts... I will miss her not. Take this reward as a token for being the forest champion.$B$B<Maggran rubs the wound caused by Besseleth.>$B$BPerhaps now many more will travel to Sun Rock Retreat without fearing what lurks in the dark.',70862),
(6285,'Great, you brought the armor!  We\'ll get this divvied to those who need it immediately.$B$BThank you, $N.  Your efforts have been a great help to us.  And now that you\'re no stranger to gryphons, I hope you\'ll come and lend your aid to Sentinel Hill often!',70862),
(6301,'Ah, $N, you have the Gaea seeds. Watch and see how the blessing of the Earthmother can cause even these small kernels of life to bloom and flourish.$B$B<Tammra begins to chant.>',70862),
(6321,'Ah, an order for supplies.  You will want to take this to the Undercity, no doubt.  And quickly, for the Sepulcher must not be left under stocked.',70790),
(6322,'This crate must reach the Sepulcher in Silverpine?  That is easily done; our bats fly there daily.',70790),
(6323,'An order from the Sepulcher?  Very well.  It is an honor to serve those who serve our Dark Lady.',70790),
(6324,'Good work, $N.  These weapons will ensure our Deathguards don\'t get caught unprepared.$B$BYou have done a valuable service for our Dark Lady.',70245),
(6365,'You have to get this meat to Orgrimmar?  That is no problem.  For a small fee, my wind rider can take you there.',70862),
(6381,'This is great victory for the land. In time, other things will come to pass: the Venture Co. will pack up their buzz saws and axes, the angry fire spirits will calm, and the harpies will be pushed out by the land.$B$BOnly then $N, will Stonetalon be truly at peace.$B$BYou have done well $c; take one of these items as thanks for the new life you have created here today.',70862),
(6382,'Welcome to the new frontier, $N.  Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young $c like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle.  Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.$B$BYour presence here tells me that you\'ve come to learn more about the hunt.  Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.',70862),
(6383,'There are three legendary creatures that make up the Ashenvale Hunt; you may seek them and test yourself against their cunning and might.  In the process, you will hopefully learn something about yourself.  The creatures are: the bear Ursangous, the nightsaber cat Shadumbra, and the hippogryph Sharptalon.$B$BThe creatures of the Ashenvale Hunt are powerful, and you may find that you\'ll need aid in bringing them down.  If you should best them, bring me proof of your deed.',70862),
(6384,'Oh, wonderful!  Those are fine cuts!  These are from Zargh, are they?  That orc sure knows his way into a lady\'s heart...$B$BOh, I can\'t wait to cook it.  But not too much!  Meat is best served rare, don\'t you think?',70862),
(6385,'You have to get this to the Crossroads in the Barrens?  Yes, I can get you there...',70862),
(6386,'Hah!  I guess she liked it!  Nothing brings red to a lady\'s cheeks like a big, juicy steak!$B$BThank you, $N.  You\'ve done me a great service.  Here is some money for your trouble, and don\'t be surprised if I invite you to my wedding!',70862),
(6387,'You have to get this to Ironforge, eh?  For a small fee I can put you on the back of one of my gryphons, and it\'ll take you there.  How does that sound?',70338),
(6391,'Ah, the lastest list of Brock\'s best pupils.  I have a batch of honorary picks ready to go.  I just need to chisel in the names of the students...',70338),
(6393,'The water spirits within me bubble with the excitement. $N, you have given me a glorious victory to report to the Tribunal of the Tides.',70862),
(6394,'Great, you got it!  Thanks a lot, $N.  This is my favorite pick!  Now if my peons ever finish chopping down these trees, maybe we can find a nice cave to mine!',70790),
(6395,'You have done a good deed today, $N.  Although our struggle against the Scourge continues, let us hope that Marla and Samuel will find peace together in their final resting place. As a token of my gratitude, please take one of these manuals I found.',70862),
(6401,'My goodness, my niece Kaya is alive! That is good news indeed. Thank you, $N.$B',70862),
(6421,'Ah... Yes! That\'s it; the Resonite crystals have a trace of Earthen magic. The kobolds must have dug deep uncovering an Earthen.$B$BLegend states that the Earthen are creatures created by the Titans.  They were used to create the land our feet walk on. This most definitely is a threat that cannot be ignored.$B$B<Mor\'rogal shakes his head.>$B$BPerhaps I can enchant these ore samples to use against this kobold plot.',70338),
(6441,'These are perfect, $N! Thanks for helping me out!$B$BOh, and this is for your time...',70862),
(6442,'We could use more of your kind around here, $N. Thank you for your help.',70862),
(6461,'Sweet, mon! Good news, perhaps we will have fewer unwanted dinner guests tonight.$B$BMany thanks, $N.  We are forever in your debt.',70862),
(6462,'You found them!  Thank you!  Thank you, $N!  You do not know how great a thing you have done for me.$B$BA $r without her charm is like an orc without her battle scars...$B$BWorthless.',70862),
(6481,'You bear good news, $c! I fear the possibilities of what an Earthen would mean to Kalimdor.$B$BSlaying Goggeroc was a task for no one less than a hero. You have done well; all of Stonetalon and Kalimdor are indebted to you, noble $c.$B$BAccept this as your reward most honored one.',70338),
(6482,'You found my brother!  He was captured by the Thistlefurs?  That is terrible news to hear, for although many Furbolgs are noble creatures, the Thistlefurs are corrupt.$B$BThank you for rescuing my brother, $N.  I do not want to think of how they treated poor Ruul.  He will likely sleep long after this ordeal...',70862),
(6503,'Very good, $N.  Your hunting skills are impressive...$B$BThe loss of those outrunners helps blind the Alliance, and when they lack intelligence they are less likely to launch attacks.',70862),
(6504,'Reading isn\'t my strong point... but now I\'ll be able to get back to work! Thanks, $N!',70862),
(6522,'I recognize the insignia on this scroll, $N. You found this on that crone who reigns over Razorfen Kraul? Interesting.$B$BThe Scourge aren\'t content with one continent it seems. This Ambassador Malcin--the one who wrote the note--is one of the Scourge\'s plagued servants, a human diplomat to the kingdom of Lordaeron before things... changed.$B$BIf the Scourge are trying to gain a foothold in Kalimdor, then it is up to us to act.',70862),
(6523,'Kaya is alive! $N, I have you to thank for rescuing her.$B',70862),
(6541,'Ashenvale is a divided land, but our most recent efforts have been very successful. We not only have an outpost at the Zoram Strand, but another just north of here called Splintertree.',70862),
(6544,'So Torek\'s attack was successful!  Well done, $N.  Night elves are decent foes.  A little skinny, but strong and fierce!  I\'m sure the battle was something to see...$B$BAnd I hope you gained a scar or two!',70862),
(6545,'Well, my update will explain all of this to Kadrak. You must return this to him as quickly as possible.',70862),
(6546,'Take my update to Kadrak. Swiftly, $N.',70862),
(6547,'Let Kadrak know of the success we have had here holding off the night elves. Our plans are going well.',70862),
(6548,'$N, I thank you... but I will never forget what the Grimtotem have done to my village.',70862),
(6561,'Kelris has eluded the Argent Dawn for some time.$B$BFor some time they considered him dead or missing.$B$BBy ending his reign you have spared the lives of many innocent people, $N.$B$BEarthmother be praised! To sacrifice another to a servant of an Old God for personal gain is beyond disgusting!$B$BYou have done a great thing this day. Kelris was a creature of evil and sought to bring the world back to a time of chaos by worshipping such creatures as the Old Gods. Thank you, $N.',70862),
(6562,'Tsunaman sent you? Excellent. Then we have matters to discuss.',70862),
(6563,'Well done, $N. These are the crystals I spoke of. Intriguing...$B$BI can feel the power within them. The spirits of water cling to them. Whatever the naga were going to use these for... well, let us be glad they are no longer in their hands.',70862),
(6564,'This is interesting indeed. I am glad you have brought it to my attention.$B$BNow we have a name for our troubles... Lorgus Jett.',70862),
(6565,'Very good!! Thank you, $N. We may not have stopped the Twilight\'s Hammer completely, but at least you have staved off another of their plans to return the Old Gods to power.$B$BWho knows what other plans they have manifesting, but we can rest easy for now.',70862),
(6621,'Good work, $N.  Issuing that challenge to the Foulwealds and defeating their leader sends them a strong message:$B$BThe Horde is not to be trifled with.$B$BI don\'t believe that tribe will be giving us much trouble for a long time.',70862),
(6629,'Grundig Darkcloud is dead! $N, I will always be grateful for what you\'ve done here today.',70862),
(6641,'I have witnessed many naga attacks since I arrived here. It puts my mind at ease that Vorsha will no longer roam freely.$B$BWe are in your debt, $N.',70862),
(6921,'This is exactly what I need!  A fathom core is an incredible well of information that we will be able to draw much good from.  Whatever the Twilight\'s Hammer is up to in there - and believe me when I say it is no good - my comrades and I will now uncover.$B$BYou\'ve done well here today; the Earthen Ring looks upon you warmly for assisting us.  You\'ve also helped the Horde as a whole, and for that you should be proud.',70862),
(6922,'This... this is quite the find, $N.$B$BYou acquired this from Baron Aquanis in Blackfathom, you say?  Baron Aquanis has long been thought of as a corrupted elemental power; this globe will prove what exactly had corrupted him.  While it would be no surprise if it turned out to be the Twilight\'s Hammer, our studies will also show how they did it as well.$B$BYou did well in bringing this to me.  Please - take this, along with the Earthen Ring\'s warmest regards.',70862),
(6981,'Oh... I have never seen anything like this...',70790),
(7383,'To be in the presence of the Oracle Tree... it is almost to feel wisdom take form. Let me continue the telling...$B$BWith Teldrassil grown, the Arch Druid approached the dragons for their blessings, as the dragons had placed upon Nordrassil in ancient times. But Nozdormu, Lord of Time, refused to give his blessing, chiding the druid for his arrogance. In agreement with Nozdormu, Alexstrasza also refused Staghelm, and without her blessing, Teldrassil\'s growth has been flawed and unpredictable...',70790),
(78142,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70862),
(78143,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70790),
(78145,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70790),
(78149,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70862),
(78150,'Thanks to your donations, the library is thriving.$B$BPlease, take this.',70862),
(79007,'As you stumble upon the remnants of yet another charred corpse, your gaze falls upon a message secured to a wooden plank.',70862),
(79094,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70790),
(79095,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70790),
(79096,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70790),
(79097,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70790),
(79192,'Backcountry adventurers and mercenaries alike undoubtedly make camp here. The corner of a note flapping in the breeze catches your eye and you reach for it.',70862),
(79361,'I can feel their corruption from here. The twisted elementals the quilboar are summoning should be drawn to the cleansing ritual.',70338),
(79365,'Our wind riders have found something, but they have been unable to get close enough to assess the situation. Were you able to find anything that might help us?',70338),
(79366,'The rumbling ground fell silent and in my heart I knew you had saved us. You have our gratitude, $N. You do your Earthen Ring proud.',70338),
(79442,'Ah, this be a powerful artifact, friend! I haven\'t crafted with some\'ting like this in a long time.$B$BYou take good care o\' dis now, ya here? Looks like ya went through plenty to get it!',70338),
(79949,'Thank you, $N. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.$B$BIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.',70862),
(79974,'Dwarven Engineering, always a marvel.',70862),
(79975,'A campfire is newly fed with wood, but signs of a quick departure are evident.',70862),
(79976,'Heavy canvas is rolled over assorted equipment. You help yourself to the pack.',70862),
(79980,'You pull a messenger bag out of the ground. Stuffed in with the supplies is a dirty parchment.',70862),
(86576,'Ah, you have brought sunstones that the harpies collect! The harpies love to gather objects that are shiny, but they do not know the true value of the stones. By capturing the dazzling light of the sun, these stones reflect its majesty and allow us to adorn our shrines and homes with tiny motes of light in its honor. The moon, too, illuminates them with its silver beauty at night.$B$BThese stones remind us of the connection we have to the lights of the skies.',70862),
(86585,'You found Ylva\'s body? Ah, the poor woman. She said she was going to show the troggs that Ironforge would never fall to their kind. She went looking for a few mountaineers who never returned from a patrol through trogg country. She was always too independent-minded to be cautious. Now we know what happened.$B$BI\'ll take the banner back and make sure it\'s cleaned up and displayed. You should take her weapon. May it serve you well against the troggs.',70338),
(86667,'This jar is for me?$B$BSnow! Grenhild did it! She sent the snow that I asked for!$B$BA pity, though, I was hoping she would come and visit in person.$B$BWell, regardless, thank you for your effort. This is a real help for my work.',70338),
(86784,'Extra firewood? That is always welcome. It will keep these old bones warm through the cold nights of the Glades.$B$BI have a sling for collecting wood myself, so you might as well hang onto that basket.',70862),
(87288,'Oh, these are wonderful. It is a shame to resort to violence with such majestic animals, but it is important to keep the roads safe, and these pelts will make beautiful blankets and shawls.$B$BHere, let me give you something to remember them. It is both soft and sturdy.',70790),
(90902,'Pain is nothing new to those who have endured death, and as such the Forsaken are particularly hardy to it. Pain has a purifying property as well that you should embrace as a badge of honor and evidence that you are, in fact, still a servant of the light despite your new circumstances. $B$BBe well and walk in the light once more, $c.',70334),
(91208,'Tragically, more than a few of our brothers and sisters succumb to a similar madness after being risen. As precious as every Forsaken soul is, sometimes the best we can do is grant those that cannot acclimate a clean end.$B$BI will say a prayer to the light for her. Thank you for doing what must be done, $N.',70334),
(91723,'Well done, my friend. Let me try my calibrations again...',70790),
(91724,'It seems like everything is working properly. Thank you, $N.',70862),
(91725,'Oh, that\'s a relief! It looks like it\'s all here. Thank you!',70862),
(91732,'Oh, very nice. Do you see that shine? Truly, they don\'t make them like they used to.',70790),
(91741,'Hey! How did you end up with that? It\'s supposed to be on the shelf! Oh dear, the kobolds have been stealing my books again. They must want to eat them!$B$BThanks for bringing back the book, but what will I do about the rest of my missing collection?',70790),
(91743,'Thank you so much! Here! Take one of these how-to books. I don\'t need them.$B$BBut there are still so many books missing. The kobolds don\'t seem to be eating them. So, why do they want them?',70790),
(91751,'Excellent work collecting these pelts, $c. You have a real talent for hunting.',70790),
(91899,'Thank you for your hard work, $N. There has been an uprising in bandits and thieves intercepting trade routes as of late. If you find other crates lying around, please bring them here and we\'ll handle the rest.$B$BHere is your payment.',70338);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(91920,'The potion didn\'t work? Of course it didn\'t work. You brought me insufficient hearts. The recipe clearly calls for six. You brought three.$B$BHowever, I confess I hadn\'t considered applications for murloc parts until now...$B$B<Renferrel takes the eyes.>$B$BI can afford to sacrifice a few of my own hearts to get your Deathstalker\'s strength back.',70862),
(91921,'<Quinn takes the potion and drinks it.>$B$BYes, I can feel it working. I will soon be able to travel.$B$BYou have done me a great favor, $N.',70862),
(92124,'Yah, I overheard. I warned Brother Paxton three times about the kobolds tunneling under the abbey.$B$BIt looks like the kobolds have taken a lot of books. There are whole bookshelves emptied out. You should probably see what Brother Paxton wants you to do about it.$B$BWhile you\'re here, can I talk to you about tradeskills? I\'d be happy to answer any questions you have, or point you toward the local trainers.',70790),
(92401,'What I asked of you was not fair, nor would it have been unjust for you to simply walk away. Thank you stranger. I am unable to repay you in kind but I hope one of these is acceptable.$B$BI hope our paths cross again without such sorrow.',70862),
(92421,'Let those who fall from the Banshee Queen\'s grace meet our justice!$B$BWith these parts, our brothers and sisters have hope to see another day. You do Captain Bandarion proud.',70790),
(92422,'While I have no doubt something of his kind will be replaced, we can only hope their ranks thin in the meantime.$B$BThank you $N.',70790),
(92434,'It is surely no coincidence the horde has taken an interest in my city during such a precarious time.$B$BIn fact, I was counting on it. I have a proposition for you.',70862),
(92460,'Gale\'s greetings, $N. I am honored to bestow your coming of age relic today as you are recognized for the potential you bring to the shen\'dorei. Our people have faced great hardship and persecution in our complex history.$B$BToday you are given this relic which is one of many held by those before you. Someday when your ashes are scattered to the winds it will pass to another to continue our tradition.$B$BAs you take this relic with you know that the winds of home will be with you wherever you travel.',70790),
(92461,'Thank you for your service to Zephras, young $c.$B$BThe vuldren are typically quite docile, but the animals that call Zephras home can sense when the magic on the winds is out of balance, which can lead to dangerous and unpredictable behavior if left unchecked.',70790),
(92462,'Judging by the amount of bug entrails covering you, this must be quite the infestation.',70790),
(92463,'Excellent work, $N. You\'d make a fine ranger if this whole "adventurer" thing doesn\'t work out for you.',70790),
(92464,'Rorian sent you? Good. I could use your aid.',70790),
(92465,'It pains me to shed shen\'dorei blood here in the grove, but we do what we must.',70790),
(92469,'This is most troubling, but unfortunately unsurprising. We\'ve been aware of the cult\'s movements for some time, but we\'ve been content to watch from afar. Their agitation of the wind spirits near the standing stones is a clear escalation on their part.$B$BYou\'ve performed a difficult but necessary service for Thendal Grove, $N. Thank you.',70790),
(92470,'Very well done. You\'ve felled beasts and laid low cultist interlopers. You have shown great promise but your path must soon take you beyond the relative safety of Thendal Village.',70790),
(92471,'Rorian has told me much of you. I am likely unknown to you, but I am a member of the Council of Elders here on Zephras Isle. I\'ve come to read the flow of the winds here in Thendal Grove. I\'m also here to assess young shen\'dorei such as yourself that are coming of age.$B$BSo tell me, are you ready to take your next step? Are you ready to serve Zephras Isle?',70790),
(92472,'Aetheen sent you, then? I\'ll confess, you don\'t look like much to me, but Shen\'dar Village won\'t turn down willing aid, much less aid sent from Elder Aetheen herself.',70790),
(92473,'Well done, $c. The Rangers of the Grove are in your debt.',70790),
(92474,'How many times do I need to tell Myriaal not to encourage others to make reckless usage of our skyborne gifts!$B$BThat being said, I suppose that a little bit of practice in the relative safety of the village is... acceptable.$B$BIn the future I\'d simply suggest you to use your ability judiciously. You do not want to exhaust your magic thoughtlessly and then not be able to use it when you truly need it.',70790),
(92482,'The way of the $c is fraught with danger, and only those with the keenest senses and quickest reflexes can thrive in the wilds. I look at you and I am reminded of myself when I stood before my mentor, so many years ago. I believe that you have what it takes, but in the end that is up to you alone.$B$BSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps.',70245),
(92484,'Can you hear it? The whispers of the winds? Doubtful, considering that the spirits stopped speaking with us when they left us those years ago. $B$BThose among us who would seek audience with the spirits of the four winds once more hone our understanding of the elements and the natural world, dearly hoping to reestablish the dialogue that was so abruptly ended. $B$BWould you walk this path and master the elements?$B$BSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps and I will train you.',70338),
(92485,'The flora and fauna of Zephras Isle represent a rich tapestry of vibrant life. The ecosystem requires constant balance to maintain the harmony of nature, and we druids are the keepers of that balance. I see much potential in you, but this path is not an easy one, and you will need guidance as you grow in strength as a student of the fang, the claw, the feather, and the branch. $B$BSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps.',70790),
(92514,'Checked in with Illaya then? Great. Lots of tension between the High Order and the Windshapers these days, but they keep things civil here in Shen\'dar. Everyone here is well aware that we\'ve got bigger problems than their quibbles.$B$BNow that that\'s done, you look like someone who might be looking for something to do with their hands and I\'ve got a bandit problem that I was hoping you could help me with.',70790),
(92515,'I didn\'t say it wouldn\'t be a dirty job, did I?',70790),
(92516,'Well done, and quickly too. Not too bad at all.',70790),
(92517,'With the bandits dispersed, that is one less problem for us to deal with. Though I confess that now I worry that any bandits who survived may turn next to the cult for protection, further bolstering their increasingly alarming numbers.$B$BStill though, we\'ll take the victories where we can get them.',70790),
(92528,'Lorthuna herself was there? She\'s the leader of the whole damned cult!$B$BIf they are making a move on Shen\'dar Village and the western watchtower, we\'ve got to be ready. What is strange is... why the watchtower?$B$BThe Village I can understand, but the tower? It doesn\'t have much strategic significance, other than as a minor lookout post.$B$BRegardless, we will be prepared for them. They\'ll find that highlanders aren\'t as easy to catch flat footed as they might think.',70790),
(92529,'What is this? A new acolyte seeking to serve the windlord sent by sister Sania? Truly we are blessed by the touch of the four winds this day!$B$BWe welcome all who seek to bask in the blessings of Al\'Akir.',70790),
(92544,'It was all I could do to stop myself from going over and joining you from my position here. I can only hope that these louts got the message and clear out of here soon. $B$BThank you, $c. You have the gratitude of the Rangers of Thendal Grove.',70790),
(92550,'Thank the winds you\'ve returned!$B$BSania Silverstream snuck out of town just before you returned, no doubt fleeing at the sight of our people arming themselves.$B$BYou\'ve done an incredible thing for the people of Shen\'dar Village and we owe you a debt of gratitude. If the cult returns to the highlands, they will find that Shen\'dar is not such an easy target.$B$BWinds guide you, $N.',70790),
(92551,'This is great! We\'ve been barely squeaking by without our regular supply deliveries. I\'ll work with the constable to ensure that these supplies get redistributed to the townsfolk who are in most dire need.',70790),
(92553,'These eggs aren\'t easy to get but wind save me, they are DELICIOUS fried up in a bit of ursera tallow.$B$BIf you\'ve got a bit of time to spare and you enjoy cooking, I can teach you a few tips and tricks I\'ve picked up. Say the word and I\'d be happy to train you.',70790),
(92579,'<Valennia\'s expression darkens as she reads the letter.>$B$BAonda trusted you to deliver this and she speaks highly enough of you in this letter, so I\'ll try to trust you too. Before we speak further, I need to consult with the few peacekeepers we have left here and formulate a plan in case the cult strikes here next. Enjoy your stay in Valanaar for now.$B$BIf you are looking to keep yourself busy, there are plenty of townsfolk that can likely use the help of a strong young adventurer like yourself.',70790),
(92595,'I think you now understand how important the mission of the Windshapers is. Every soul who commands the skysight is of vital importance if we hope to establish dialogue with the spirits of the winds once again.$B$BBetween threats from within such as the Al\'Aketh, and the uncertainty of our safety here in Skywall, it is our responsibility as Windshapers to use our gifts to save our home and ensure that the Shen\'dorei can survive these trying times.',70790),
(92596,'The High Order\'s mission is vital to the survival of our people. We hold our elemental benefactors in the utmost regard, but we must face reality; they are gone now, and we are on our own.$B$BBetween threats from within such as the Al\'Aketh, and uncertainties of our security on this plane, it is our destiny as Highborne descendants of our ancestral home of Eldre\'Thalas to use our gifts to ensure that the shen\'dorei can stand on our own once again.',70245),
(92597,'Do you feel it? Yes? Good! You have taken your first steps. You\'ll find that with your abilities, you will be able to tap into latent magical energy in many locations. Doing so will provide a myriad of benefits, some profound, others more subtle. You won\'t know until you tap into them, but that\'s the best part of the gift... making the unknown known.$B$BIf we are to survive these dire times, we must be unwavering in our search for knowledge... and power.',70245),
(92598,'Like a muscle, your skysight must be exercised if you hope to grow stronger in the gift. Leveraging your skysight to bridge the distance between the mortal and the spiritual may prove invaluable to you in your adventures.$B$BYou\'d do well to remember what you\'ve learned here today. Our ability to use our gifts to hear what the elements tell us could be the key to our survival.',70790),
(92640,'Tensions between the Windshapers and High Order are high right now, but we couldn\'t hope to carry out this plan without both groups on board.',70790),
(92642,'You are still alive? Thank the winds for small miracles, I suppose.',70790),
(92643,'<This man is clearly dead, killed by the assassins that you fought outside the house. As you kneel down to inspect the body you notice the glinting reflection of something shiny...>',70790),
(92644,'The turncoat was already dead when you arrived, you say? This is unfortunate news.$B$B<You hand over the crystal you found on the dead cultist\'s body.>$B$BInteresting...',70790),
(92645,'Belguilos is dead? Four winds bless you, $c. $B$BWe might just make it out of this alive after all.',70790),
(92646,'I sent a few of our healers to ensure that Valennia and her remaining forces made it back in one piece. She should be resting in the High Elder\'s residence now.$B$BMuln has already departed back to Azeroth, but he and I spoke of what is next for the Windshapers and our mission to Azeroth. Unfortunately, the island is more vulnerable than ever now and we need a plan to protect Zephras from what is to come.',70790),
(92679,'<Aamelia listens while you explain what became of Alvarion.>$B$BAt least I know he\'s going to be safe in Valanaar.$B$BStranger, I hate to tell you this but I think my idiot husband likely just sent you here to die for nothing. If you have any sense at all, you should leave now. This isn\'t your fight.',70790),
(92682,'I watched you take down those bandits from the window. Not bad.',70790),
(92683,'This stuff can be a bit messy and it tends to get everywhere. You\'ll probably be shaking this out of your trousers for weeks, unfortunately. I do appreciate it, though. I\'ve had this on my to-do list for weeks, but getting too far from the house when it\'s just me on my own with bandits lurking everywhere is a big risk.$B$BDon\'t bother asking me what I use this stuff for. Things. Stuff and things. Don\'t worry about it.',70790),
(92684,'These are big tenderloins! You must have taken down some real monsters out there.',70790),
(92685,'When I said the bloodier the better, you really listened. Good. It lets me know you made it hurt.$B$BOn a serious note, thank you for what you\'ve done so far. I\'ve been floating aimlessly around this farm for weeks as if I was just waiting for the end to come. I think I\'m starting to have hope again.$B$BFerauu and his thugs are due any time now. All that\'s left is to go out and face them. What do you say, will you see this through to the end with me?',70790),
(92693,'I... can\'t believe it\'s over. I need to stop and calm myself before my heart leaps right out of my chest.',70790),
(92698,'The construct? It\'s been wandering around the fields for decades. Since the wind elementals left us, I think. Alvarion suspected that it used to haul harvests to market, or maybe tend to livestock back before this was an orchard. That could have been a thousand years ago though.$B$BIn the old days, the Windshapers used to maintain these constructs. We\'ve talked about petitioning them to come and take a look at it, but it\'s never been a pressing concern to us. Mostly we just ignore it these days.',70790),
(92699,'Hello and welcome. Rathiril sent me a magical missive about you and he mentioned you had some promise.$B$BWith you standing before me now, I can see why he suggested you seek me out. You have a vibrant arcane aura about you. Few enough of us anymore have the aptitude, let alone the will, to do what is needed to save our home. Do you have the boldness and strength needed to aid the High Order?$B$BI suppose we will see.',70245),
(92700,'Elder Amberwind sent me a message about you and your exploits in Shen\'dar Village. You are most welcome here, friend.$B$BYou have a strong aura, and you clearly have a resonance with the spirits. Fewer and fewer of us have the skysight of late, and Zephras needs those with the gift if we are to survive these trying times. I am glad you have found your way to me.$B$BI look forward to further making your acquaintance.',70790),
(92701,'<Valennia\'s expression darkens as she reads the letter.>$B$BAonda trusted you to deliver this and she speaks highly enough of you in this letter, so I\'ll try to trust you too. Before we speak further, I need to consult with the few peacekeepers I have left here and formulate a plan in case the cult strikes here next. Enjoy your stay in Valanaar for now.$B$BIf you are looking to keep yourself busy, there are plenty of townsfolk that can likely use the help of a strong young adventurer like yourself.',70245),
(92703,'<Alvarion\'s eyes tear up as you finish retelling the story of what happened at the orchard.>$B$BI don\'t know how to thank you, friend. I came to Valanaar looking for hope. A vain hope, I was almost certain. But instead I found a hero. A real hero, like the stories from before we came to Skywall. $B$BI\'ll never forget what you did for us, $N. You\'ll always be welcome at the Windfield home.',70790),
(92706,'Finally, somebody killed that thing! Do you know how hard it is to get a crew in the water when everyone in town\'s crying "Shark!" all the time?$B$BI might just put that monster\'s fin into a soup for dinner tonight, just to have the last laugh.',70790),
(92708,'So now you see? There is a world of knowledge and untapped potential outside of Skywall. This will never stop being our home, but I\'ve come to believe that the path to our salvation lies below. We must travel to Azeroth and gain the power and means to save Zephras Isle. This is the way.$B$BWill you have the courage to join us when the time comes?',70790),
(92709,'So do you now see? Rediscovering the ancient magic of our forebears is the key to unlocking the secrets of Zephras Isle and securing our future, but in order to save our home, we must rediscover what we\'ve lost these past millennia.$B$BAzeroth is the key. The Kirin Tor will show us the way.$B$BWhile we make ready to leave, you should check in with the other members of the High Order here in Valanaar. Most of them have tasks that they could use help from one such as yourself to see completed.',70245),
(92727,'<The satchel lying before you has a few specks of what appears to be dried blood on the flap. Studying the stain, you notice that the flap also has a name embroidered onto it. It reads "Fillion Flamebreeze".>',70245),
(92741,'That is quite the haul of talons you\'ve brought me. I cannot wait to dig into this!$B$BThank you for your service to the High Order, $c.',70245),
(92742,'Thank you. Let me see...',70862),
(92744,'I see... these gills appear to be healthy, for now. But we must not be complacent.',70862),
(92745,'Well done, $N. But I fear the source of the poison may lie somewhere else...',70862),
(92747,'What is all this?',70862),
(92748,'Need something blown up?',70862),
(92749,'This is a great start! Now to tie it all together... and add a little extra zing...',70862),
(92750,'Hmm... Looking for something specific, are you?',70862),
(92751,'Great--that\'s exactly what we need!',70862),
(92752,'I\'m glad you\'ve returned, $N.',70862),
(92753,'So you found the forge, and planted the bomb... only one thing remains to be done.',70862),
(92819,'I don\'t know what to say, $N. To think that Stormwind would put their military ambitions over the livelihood of their people...',70862),
(92834,'The High Order prides ourselves in our pragmatism and logic, and logic dictates that the avoidance of conflict and loss of life is the most prudent option in most situations.$B$B<Elaadrin\'s eyes begin to glow and crackle with arcane energy.>$B$B...however, the cult mistook our prudence for weakness and they are not nearly ready to pay the cost of that error.',70245),
(92840,'It would not have been my preference to spill Windshaper blood but the blame for this pointless conflict rests solely on their shoulders. We sought to peacefully gather information, and they responded with violence.$B$BUnfortunately, word has spread and the Windshapers are already calling it a \'massacre\'. They wouldn\'t dare to retaliate here in Valanaar, but they will certainly not forget.$B$B$N, you have been of tremendous aid to the High Order. Thank you.',70245),
(92849,'Th... thank you, stranger. I was returning from an assignment at the Overlook Standing Stones when I was suddenly ambushed and attacked by Windshapers. They forced me over to the mouth of the cave and left me there, barely conscious and bleeding. The last thing I remember before blacking out is a massive winged beast emerging from the cave and scooping me up.$B$BI think it\'s safe to say that if you hadn\'t come along, I\'d have been dinner for that beast and its younglings.',70245),
(92850,'Thank you again, $N.',70245),
(92860,'I am sorry to hear about Belathaan. He was actually my cousin and he was a good mage and servant of Zephras. We will avenge him.$B$BYou seem eager to lend aid immediately. Come, let\'s speak further on the current situation.',70245),
(92871,'You seem eager to lend aid immediately. Come, let\'s speak further on the current situation.',70790),
(92880,'<Valennia looks visibly relieved as you tell her about the status of the eastern watchtower.>$B$BThank the winds.',70790),
(92881,'I have a small matter that requires just the kind of assistance that an adventurer like yourself can provide.',70790),
(92909,'Thanks a bunch! I\'ll get to work on an escape plan. In the meantime, take this!',70862),
(92947,'We fought hard to get this far but it isn\'t over yet.',70790),
(93036,'Greetings child, my name is Sania Silverstream and I am a junior priestess in the Order of the Al\'Aketh. Do you wish to learn more of our sovereign, the Windlord Al\'Akir?$B$BThere is always room at the Windlord\'s table for the righteous and the repentant.',70790),
(93065,'We are as ready as we\'ll ever be.',70790),
(93089,'It gladdens me to hear that we have High Elder Shadowsong\'s blessing for our expedition. Now that the cult has been defeated and preparations have been made, I think it\'s finally time.$B$BAnsirem has worked diligently to help us get stable skycutter transport going between the city of Dalaran and Zephras Isle. We\'ve done as much testing as we can, and the time has come for our vanguard to depart.',70245),
(93090,'I\'m pleased to hear that we have High Elder Shadowsong\'s blessing for our expedition. Now that the cult has been defeated and preparations have been made, I think it\'s finally time.$B$BMuln has worked diligently to help us get stable skycutter transport going between Zephras Isle and a place called Mulgore, where the Earthen Ring make their home. We\'ve been doing test voyages and some of our people are already waiting on the other side.',70790),
(93159,'...that\'s about all I have to say about it. I was--um--somewhere else before I was here. Now I\'m here and I have my friends, and my things. T-things I built, I mean. That\'s about all I need. I think that\'s all I need, anyway.$B$BI have to say though, it is nice to talk to someone who will talk back. The forest spirits try, but they just end up singing at me. That\'s nice in its own way, but not exactly s-stimulating conversation.',70790),
(93160,'Thank you, stranger! You\'ll find that these are delicious once roasted! $B$BPlease excuse me, it won\'t take me long to whip this up.',70790),
(93165,'Excellent work. Only good things can happen by eliminating the cult. Hopefully this sends a message that the Nightclaw are not to be trifled with and that our resentments run deep.$B$BI suspect you have your work cut out for yourself, taking on the cult. If you gather more ears, bring them here.',70790),
(93172,'Thank you, stranger.',70790),
(93317,'Winds bless me, this meat looks fantastic! $B$BThank you so much, $c.',70790),
(93318,'If we didn\'t have enough on our plates between the cult and the highlands bandits, we don\'t need a giant vuldren terrorizing our citizens as well. You\'ve done a great thing here today. As promised, here is your reward.',70790),
(93319,'Thanks $c. This should help us get by for now. If we can\'t get the supply routes squared away soon though, a few stolen windstones will be the least of our worries.',70790),
(93320,'We are holding them off for now, but they have greater numbers and our fighters are starting to get tired. We need to do something to break the stalemate, and do it fast.',70790),
(93461,'Checked in with Rathiril then? Great. Lots of tension between the High Order and the Windshapers these days, but they keep things civil here in Shen\'dar. Well, at least in the village anyway. What happens out in the wilds stays in the wilds.$B$BNow that that\'s done, you look like someone who might be looking for something to do with their hands. I\'ve got a few things that need doing, if you are game for a bit of work?',70245),
(93552,'Thank you very much for these. As elves we all have a deep connection to magic and these windstones are becoming more and more precious as the magic imbued into this island by the great anchor pylons continues to fade. $B$BWindstones aren\'t the only beneficial thing you can harvest from the land. Please, take one of these manuals.',70790),
(93680,'A sewer key? Well, thankfully I am not the one who will be using this.$B$BBut we have work to do before it\'s safe to use this.',70862),
(93735,'<Riaani\'s face is buried under the heaving armor plates of the construct, attempting to work on the mechanisms underneath. He does not notice your presence at all.>$B$BStorms curse--where is the core?! Who thought it would be a good idea to remove the Gyrozephyr as well? It\'s a miracle this construct\'s winds haven\'t dissipated entirely by now!',70790),
(93736,'Handling these essences fills me with a sense of... deep disquiet. I can almost feel a malevolent, regretful aura emanating from them. It\'s enough to make me faint.$B$B<Endaria shudders slightly.>$B$BI do not look forward to studying these further.',70790),
(93737,'Thank you for scavenging these materials. I imagine that some of this wasn\'t terribly easy to get. $B$BWith these parts I can get the construct up and running again. From there we can just hope that its memory is intact and it can tell us who took its components.',70790),
(93738,'Very interesting, so it was the High Order that was responsible for the construct breaking down?$B$BI know Belathaan. He\'s Valennia Stormfist\'s cousin and his mother was actually a Windshaper. It\'s disappointing that he was involved in this.$B$BI need to reflect on this for a moment.',70790),
(93739,'So you have returned. I hope that you learned much in your journey.$B$BIt is my understanding that your people are still establishing themselves in Mulgore. While you wait for them, I\'d encourage you to explore the territory around Orgrimmar. The Barrens in particular is always in need of eager adventurers like yourself.',70790);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(93740,'<Ayessa looks shaken and distant as you hand her the windstone charms.>$B$BDon\'t mind me, $N. Today has merely been... a trying day. Thank you for your service to the windshapers thus far.',70790),
(93746,'Wait--what?! Belathaan... is dead? $B$B<Ayessa listens as you give your account of what occurred.> $B$BThe High Order was meeting with the Al\'Aketh to discuss peace? There is no peace with the cult, they are murderous zealots. What was Elaadrin thinking sending Belathaan to treat with them alone?$B$BPay this no mind, $N. You are not at fault for this. The arrogance of the High Order is to blame, yet again. You were merely in the right place at the wrong time.',70790),
(93835,'I sent a few of our remaining mages to ensure that Valennia and her forces were able to escape as well. She should be resting at High Elder Shadowsong\'s residence now.$B$BAnsirem had to return to Azeroth, but he and I discussed the next steps for the High Order before he departed. We survived the day, but Zephras is dangerously vulnerable now and we must make plans for what is to come.',70245),
(93836,'<Talaanis Shadowsong listens intently as you tell him of what transpired above the Shrine of Akir, and of Ayessa\'s plan to leave Zephras Isle.>$B$BI need to reflect on this further, but looking at the upside, we have rid ourselves of Lorthuna and deprived the cult of their leader. Our home has not been invaded yet and on the timeline of elemental gods, it could be years... decades even, before Al\'Akir deigns to turn his attention to us.$B$BThere is much to fear now, but much to celebrate as well.',70790),
(93926,'<The body here is somewhat fresh, clearly only recently having been killed. Judging by the burns and scorch marks on this peacekeeper\'s skin, it\'s clear that they were killed by the cult\'s storm-wielding spellcasters.>',70790),
(93927,'So they are all dead, then. Storms curse these cult bastards!$B$BWhile you managed to take out the priest and stop the cultists at the tower, I confess that I\'m now doubly concerned about whatever it was you said that they were doing to the pylon. The fact that there was such a massive cache of windstones there with them tells me that they needed enormous energy for it.$B$BI have to wonder, what\'s the end goal here? Violating the pylon, attacking the village? To what end?',70790),
(93948,'I... am very sorry to hear that my nephew is dead. I thank you kindly for recovering this, and bringing it to me.$B$BIt\'s not common that such capable young shen\'dorei come down from the highlands. If you need work, please speak with Valennia Stormfist, the captain of the peacekeepers here in Valanaar. These days we need all the help we can get.',70790),
(93949,'I\'m sure there are more of these critters around Valanaar, but every enchanted skyhopper we stomp out makes the city just a tiny bit safer.',70790),
(93951,'It might seem a bit of a vain triviality, gathering feathers for our hair. However, even in times like these, one needs to embrace the small joys as much as possible. $B$BIf one thing I create brings someone joy, then I will consider that to be a good day. Thank you for bringing me these and helping me bring some joy to Zephras.',70790),
(93958,'<Valennia looks gravely wounded.>',70790),
(94006,'So, you wish to embrace the way of the claw, child? Very well. Let us speak.',70790),
(94007,'I am most glad that you came. Come, let us begin.',70291),
(94013,'Excellent, $N! You are quite a fast learner. Now that you know the basics, I can teach you how to forge a lasting bond with an animal companion.$B$BGo with this knowledge and thrive. Be the $c that Zephras Isle needs you to be.',70245),
(94050,'A fledgling $c, I see. Yes, I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.$B$BRemember, $N, always respect the balance and live in awe of nature around you. Now, go forth. We shall speak again, at a later date.',70245),
(94369,'<Talaanis Shadowsong listens intently as you tell him of what transpired above the Shrine of Akir, and of Elaadrin\'s plan to leave Zephras Isle.>$B$BI need to reflect on this further, but looking at the upside, we have rid ourselves of Lorthuna and deprived the cult of their leader. Our home has not been invaded yet, and on the timeline of elemental demigods, it could be years... decades even, before Al\'Akir deigns to turn his attention to us.$B$BThere is much to fear now, but much to celebrate as well.',70245),
(94411,'Direct conflict with our shen\'dorei brothers and sisters only weakens us as a people, but decisive action must at times be taken to prevent greater tragedy.$B$BThe mages of the High Order have zero regard for the consequences of their magical meddling. The forces that bind our island are fragile and vulnerable and all it could take is one thoughtless action to destroy our home.',70790),
(94413,'Sometimes I find it hard to distinguish between the blind zealotry of the Al\'Aketh cult, and the stubborn refusal of the Windshapers to change.$B$BIf they truly believed the winds would guide us, they should be sensing the direction the winds are blowing and flow with them rather than against them.',70245),
(94414,'Thank you for taking a moment to share this with me. I will continue to watch over the grove, and ponder on the state of our homeland.',70790),
(94484,'Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?$B$B<Elegael pales as you relay your conversation with Lotheluum.>$B$BSo the message did not get through. We are in dire straits indeed then.$B$BIt seems we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence.',70790),
(94485,'<Elegael takes the sticky mound of moss from you with a weak smile.>$B$BThank you, $N, you have done well. This is exactly what we need.',70790),
(94486,'Thank you for these. I will be sure to use every feather so their sacrifice will not be in vain.',70790),
(94487,'<Elegael looks down at the collection of bloodied heirlooms with distress.>$B$BSo many young lives with so much potential now gone forever. Thank you for returning these, $c.$B$BI will hold onto them for safekeeping until I am able to take them to the High Elder. There they can go back into the collection and await the next and perhaps more worthy generation to come of age.',70790),
(94488,'<Elegael grimaces at the severed head, but nods curtly.>$B$BThank you, $N. No matter how much rage I have within me, it would have been difficult to strike down my own cousin.$B$BDo not mourn for him. His ignorance and malice has killed many innocents this day.',70790),
(94489,'<Elegael\'s face pales as you relay the fate of Jorel and the condition of the rest of the druids.>$B$BNo... no! This is far worse than I had--$B$B<Elegael chokes back a sob and grits her teeth, letting out a pained snarl.>$B$BThey will pay. They will ALL pay. Anyone who allies with the Al\'Aketh will feel my wrath! This I swear.',70790),
(94490,'They were here for the pylon? But to what end? We were not the original reason for their attack?$B$B<Elegael trails off shaking with rage as she reads.>$B$BThey murdered my people because we were an inconvenience! I shall tear apart every cultist with my fangs! I will make sure none leave this place with their lives.$B$BGo, swiftly! If the orders truly originated in Valanaar, it means it is likely a traitor hiding there. Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valanaar and tell him what has transpired.',70790),
(94491,'<Lotheluum wears a look of genuine terror as you recount the events from the $c den.>$B$BI--I\'m sorry, $N. I need just a moment. There are no words I possess that can describe the loss.$B$BThis is grave news indeed. If this missive is not fabricated, then we indeed have at best an accomplice and at worst a traitor here in Valanaar. I will take this to the High Elder immediately! I will not let my fellows\' sacrifice be in vain.',70790),
(94568,'We could try and send peacekeepers to directly engage the cult forces, but we would not fare well against them in open battle.$B$BWe are going to need a different approach.',70790),
(94638,'The agony I feel over her loss is immeasurable, but it is what is necessary for the balance. You have demonstrated a resolve to persevere, even when a terrible price is asked.$B$BYou have done well, $c. I shall grant you the blessing to take on the shape of my kin. Be a beacon for those that lack the strength to persevere and a defender of those in need.$B$BGo now, and embrace the way of the claw, child.',70790),
(94773,'You have done the Light a great service by becoming a shining example to those who travel in these dangerous lands and beyond. Please, accept this lesson as a thanks for all you\'ve done.',70790),
(94896,'Thank you, $c, you have done a great kindness to us refugees this day. I will make sure to return these to their owners. At least it gives us a place to start over from.',70790),
(94897,'<Ealaane\'s eyes well with tears.>$B$BOh, Resaan my love. What will become of us now? There was so much... it feels as if our lives together had just started.$B$BThank you, $c. The world is cruel to take both my home and my love from me. At least his heirloom will give me some closure.',70790),
(94911,'A high elf, speaking to me... in Thunder Bluff. Will wonders never cease?$B$BWell, shaper of wind, let me join our Earthen Ring brothers and sisters in welcoming you to Azeroth. My fellow druids of the Cenarion Circle have much wisdom to impart upon you, child of nature.',70790),
(94913,'Ah I see that you have already mastered the form of the Bear. Good, good. You are well on your way, young $c.',70790),
(94946,'Ah, you\'ve made it. Wonderful. It\'s going to take us some time to get ourselves established here, so you may want to take some time to explore the city. Be warned however, try not to venture too far from the safety of the city proper.  $B$BAs idyllic as this new land appears, it can be extremely dangerous to wander outside of Dalaran without appropriate preparation and experience.',70245),
(94947,'Well met, $c. I am Bolvar Fordragon, regent to the throne of Stormwind.$B$BA Kirin Tor messenger told me to expect to receive members of the High Order, and here you stand. It\'s been some time since a high elf has stood in this throne room, but I am glad to accept you now as a guest.$B$BOn behalf of the King, I welcome you to Stormwind and give you leave to travel freely through alliance lands. Welcome to Azeroth, Skyborne.',70245),
(94978,'Well tamed, $N! You are becoming adept already.',70245),
(94979,'You\'re back already! Impressive speed, $N!',70245),
(95204,'<Oran bites the crest to ensure authenticity.>$B$BWell I\'ll be. A genuine relic of our home. Mostly intact, too. We need to be extra careful with this one.$B$BThank you for your aid in restoring our history, $c. I\'ll see to it that we take good care of this.',70790),
(95212,'These pelts will make excellent saddles. You\'ve done the Alliance proud, $c!',70338),
(95216,'You killed it??$B$BHmmph. Lucky for you this should be enough ichor to reverse engineer its properties. You do not wish to be an enemy of the Royal Apothecary Society.$B$BGet out of my sight!',70790),
(95314,'You say there is evil in Shadowvale? I admit, I am not surprised. The forest folk were an odd lot, and they did not care for visitors. Some believe the Whispering Forest itself is cursed, and the elixir distilled from its roots carries that same curse...$B$B...but enough of superstition and rumors, $N. Thank you for the elixirs. Here, take this as payment.',70245),
(95349,'More adventurers from Zephras, I see. Wonderful. The winds surely favor us! It\'s going to take us some time to get ourselves established here, so you may want to take some time to explore this new land.$B$BAzeroth is an exciting new world, but it\'s also a dangerous world. You\'d do well to prepare yourself for this new adventure by familiarizing yourself with the lands nearby.',70790),
(95350,'Lok-tar, $c. I am Thrall, Warchief of the Horde.$B$BAn Earthen Ring messenger told me to expect members of the Windshapers, and here you are. I\'d not have expected to see a high elf standing before me here in Orgrimmar, but the Horde will welcome you as our guest all the same.$B$BYou have my blessing to travel through Horde lands. Go with honor, Windshaper.',70790),
(95494,'Yes, these look like they will do nicely. I have an arrangement with a local tanner to deliver these raw hides in exchange for various finished leather goods that I use as part of my trade. $B$BI\'ve never come up short on my end of the arrangement, and even with my injury I do not intend to start now.',70862),
(95495,'Vrang sent you then? Very well. I appreciate you delivering these hides to me. It\'s unfortunate that Vrang couldn\'t make the journey himself. There is a matter I wish to speak with him about.',70862),
(95507,'Thank you for your aid, $c. I was starting to wonder if I\'d have to go to bed hungry tonight because this cursed wound on my leg.',70862),
(95508,'Well, looks like we are all alive. I... knew that someday that would catch up to me. I\'m in your debt for your help here today.$B$BPlease, take this. It\'s not much, but it\'s the least I can do.$B$BSafe travels, $c.',70862),
(95621,'So they are looking for a deserter... Well, it seems that the past has finally caught up to me.',70862),
(95663,'Arrival of the courageous few? Mind your voice.',70862),
(95664,'It is a favored sign to have a stranger approach in this manner. I feel a power amidst you... what is this you have brought?',70862),
(95682,'Don\'t mind me snatching that right out of your hands.$B$BI recognized that orcish scrawl. So they\'re hoping to appease Rend? A fruitless and wasted effort. $B$BNo matter, this is highly valuable knowledge for the dark lady to consider.$B$BHere, I won\'t be taking any of this with me--and don\'t talk about the mission, grunt.',70862),
(95697,'Look at the marbling on these! What are they eating up there? Thank you for going all the way and back for us. If you don\'t mind waiting, we\'ll cook some for you now, on the house, of course!',70862),
(95774,'I will place these adornments with Olgra\'s memorial, so that I never forget her. My blood will always run hot with revenge from this day until my last day. Each swing of my blade and enemy felled will be in her name.$B$BYou have done me... done us... a great honor. $B$BLok-tar, $N.',70862),
(95883,'<The tortured soul lets out a foul energy in the presence of the offering stone.$B$BIt appears you are closer to fulfilling the ritual.>',70790),
(95884,'<Strange implements and items litter the rough surface of the stone.$B$BThis is surely the offering stone that is mentioned in the note.>',70790),
(95885,'<The offering stone is inert now. It appears your ritual drained it of power. To what end, you do not know, but it is over now.$B$BThe rough stone cracks and crumbles, now devoid of purpose.$B$BSomething glitters from within the remnants...>',70338),
(95981,'Ever since the barrier went down around Dalaran, the Kirin Tor have maintained a death grip on the roads. They\'re paranoid about something, that much is certain.$B$BFor now, however, the why is irrelevant.',70790),
(95998,'So now that we\'ve learned the basics, why don\'t you go and learn a tradeskill. They will also teach you the know-how to create a proper camp fixture suitable to your new profession.',70790),
(96101,'So now that we\'ve learned the basics, why don\'t you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.',70790),
(96241,'Heh... when I said unique properties, I wasn\'t kiddin\' mon! You seem no worse for wear, so it be all good.$B$BThank you for your aid, $c. It be much appreciated.',70862),
(96259,'Thank you for your service to the people of this land. It may take time for us to completely clear out the infestation, but your efforts have created a stable foothold for us to leverage against these vile creatures.',70862),
(96260,'These are excellent samples, and more than sufficient for my needs.$B$BHere, take this. I was able to craft a rather unique cloak with a weave I spun from the small sample of silk already in my possession. I am hopeful that you will find it useful in your travels.$B$BEarthmother watch over you, $c.',70862),
(96261,'Reanimated dead? The broodmother possessing a night elven form? These are troubling revelations. One has to wonder what it all means... I fear that must be a concern for a later time.$B$BThank you, $N. You\'ve done the Earthen Ring and the people of Mulgore a great service.',70862),
(96294,'This is... most disturbing. Why would a druid be behind a brood of dangerous spiders? Who or what is this "Wild King" and "Pact" that is referenced in this letter?$B$BI will confer with the druids of the Cenarion Circle on this. Perhaps they will know more.$B$BThank you again for your aid. As disturbing as this information is, we will rest easier knowing that the person controlling these vile creatures has been destroyed.',70862),
(96339,'Wait, wait, you said your name was $N?$B$B$N! I am so glad to finally meet you. Someone delivered a package here addressed to you and assured me that you would eventually come to pick it up. I tried to tell them that we don\'t do that around here, but before I could get a word in, they were already gone!$B$BYour timing is great, too. It was gonna be lumped up with all the other garbage that I toss into the sea nightly.$B$BWhat? We all do it. Ugh, just take your package and go!',70291),
(96390,'These Dark Irons may be our cousins but they ain\'t family, that\'s for sure. I shed no tears for any misfortune that befalls them that stray too far from that accursed mountain o\' theirs.$B$BHopefully this is enough to put \'em off of further incursions into these lands.',70338),
(96391,'Judging by this map, it certainly looks like these Dark Irons are planning some sort of incursion into the vaults beneath Ironforge. The band ye busted up to the east must be a scouting force.$B$BThank ye for bringing me this. If we hurry, we might be able to beat them to whatever their goal is down there.',70862),
(96393,'A Dark Iron incursion--right beneath our feet? Well, I\'m relieved to hear that the Dark Iron commander has been dispatched.$B$BThe guards will head in and clean up the rest of the rabble. We\'ll see to it that the breaches are sealed and the lower levels reinforced to ensure that no further incursions are possible.$B$BThank ye for yer service to Ironforge, $c. Take this as a small token of my gratitude. Oh, and if ye see that old Wildhammer rockhugger Farsen again, tell \'em to pay me a proper visit.',70862),
(96394,'Ah good, it\'s done then. I can\'t have the other keepers refusing to enter the hall to do their duties on account of "ghosts" and "angry dead", can I?',70862),
(96395,'My... Thane... he... rests... yes... rest.$B$BThank... you...$B$BI... rest...',70862),
(96403,'Look at you, as brave as you are enterprising! I\'m a gnome of my word, and your reward is well earned! $B$BNow, let me take a look at the haul--uh, I mean... the recovered heirlooms. I need to get started appraising--excuse me, \'cataloging\' them so that they can be put back in their proper places as quickly as possible.',70862),
(96604,'So now that we\'ve learned the basics, go learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.',70840),
(96606,'So now that we\'ve learned the basics, why don\'t you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.',70790),
(96607,'So now that we\'ve learned the basics, why don\'t you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.',70862),
(96626,'With this, you\'ll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you\'ve learned is just the basics, so you won\'t be able to place too many furnishings around it.$B$BRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.$B$BYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you\'re savvy in their skills.',70790),
(96627,'I appreciate the lookin\' out, $c. That marshal\'s just a worrywart.$B$BHey, you\'ve got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?',70790),
(96634,'With this, you\'ll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you\'ve learned is just the basics, so you won\'t be able to place too many furnishings around it.$B$BRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.$B$BYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you\'re savvy in their skills.',70790),
(96638,'Well met!',70790),
(96646,'With this, you\'ll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you\'ve learned is just the basics, so you won\'t be able to place too many furnishings around it.$B$BRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.$B$BYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you\'re savvy in their skills.',70790),
(96652,'Is that my journal? I\'ve been missing this for a while. Thank you, $c.$B$BHey, you\'ve got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?',70840),
(96655,'With this, you\'ll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you\'ve learned is just the basics, so you won\'t be able to place too many furnishings around it.$B$BRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.$B$BYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you\'re savvy in their skills.',70790),
(96656,'I\'m not affiliated with the Scarlet Crusade, if you couldn\'t tell. I\'m just an adventurer stopping by before my next venture into the wilderness.$B$BHey, you\'ve got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?',70862),
(96658,'With this, you\'ll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you\'ve learned is just the basics, so you won\'t be able to place too many furnishings around it.$B$BRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.$B$BYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you\'re savvy in their skills.',70862),
(96821,'The peons have been scared to travel south for some time, $N. Now that you\'ve cleared the path a bit, we can get them back to work.',70840),
(96822,'These warriors will always be remembered, $N. You have made sure of that.',70840),
(96825,'I\'ll use these to prepare something tasty, and save the seeds for planting. Someday we\'ll have prickly pears growing all around Orgrimmar!',70862),
(96873,'Fine work. A shame about the slain trolls, but with the binding spells removed, their spirits can rest.',70840),
(96876,'My pack! When I dropped it to run from that huge spider, I thought I\'d never see it again. You really are a hero!',70790),
(96877,'What a trophy, $c! That must have been some fight!',70790),
(96895,'Stay low and try not to be seen, $c. These cultists are not to be trifled with.',70862),
(96896,'I plan to stay here for a time and speak with more of my friends, but I will return to Light\'s Hope Chapel in Eastern Plaguelands soon enough. Should you ever find yourself out that way, please do say hello. We could always use more help from able-bodied adventurers.',70790),
(96897,'Thank you for your aid, $c. If we do not wish to see Lordaeron\'s history repeat itself, we\'ve got to be vigilant when threats like this spring up.',70790),
(96898,'Thank you. This should slow the efforts of the Scourge in this area. I suspect the denizens of Tirisfal will be pulling these crystals out of the ground for years, but removing the most conspicuous of them can only help.',70790),
(96899,'This place is full of memories for me. This place was once held by the Argent Dawn. It was from here that we prepared for many battles and skirmishes against the Scourge during their most recent push into Tirisfal Glades.$B$BWhen we withdrew to the Plaguelands I feared it would fall into disrepair. My fear was well-founded, but I am glad that Danitha and her paladins have taken over stewardship of it now.$B$BShe even named the keep after... a mutual friend.',70790),
(96986,'Excellent work. That beast is unworthy to walk among the dead. Let him lie beneath them.',70338),
(96987,'I guess I shouldn\'t have sent a stooge to look for priceless artifacts. This is barely worth sellin\' at a tourist kiosk! What, did you just grab the first book that seemed to be jutting out from the rest?$B$BForget it. Maybe I can spray it with gold and say it belonged to an arch mage or somethin\'.',70338),
(97003,'Impressive, $c. None will doubt my tales when I return to Orgrimmar with this grim proof of the existence of these abominations. Rest assured this glory is yours however, and I will speak loudly of your deeds.$B$BLok-tar!',70790),
(97220,'Oh, dear. You think we want to carry that up the stairs ourselves? Keeping the valuables intact is your responsibility up until the point you drop it off.',70862),
(97222,'Yep. There\'s a reason that hinge opens inwards towards them, so they don\'t get the door blocked by people leaving stuff anywhere they please.$B$BConsider us professionally acquainted, $c. $B$BWe respect your business, and expect you to respect ours.',70862),
(97223,'Thank you, $N. I am happy we will be able to preserve her bloodline and raise them to be our allies. You have done a great service for our tribe.',70840);
INSERT INTO `eglink_offer_reward` (`ID`,`Txt`,`Build`) VALUES
(97225,'You have done a great deed for our tribe today.$B$BUnlike some tribes, our kinship with our loa is one of reverence and respect, and we owe them much.$B$BI would not want the Darkspear to fall out of favor with them.',70840),
(97236,'My, my. How I do love surprises, $N.$B$BThis specimen will surely help further my studies.',70790),
(97242,'This type of cattail and speargrass is unique to Orgrimmar. Drinking from Azshara mountain spring water, and nourished by the sweat and blood soaked mineral dust of our rocky land, these herbs contain potent powers locked within.$B$BI\'ll give these to Yelmak, who may be able to win back Whuut\'s ear with a hands-on lesson.',70862),
(97246,'Of course. Migi\'s parents and I have an arrangement to give Migi a bagged lunch every day, but I can only ensure the boy gets his food if he actually comes in to pick it up.$B$BSometimes, he doesn\'t pick up his meal multiple times a week, and I wonder where he gets the energy to stay out and play.',70790),
(97249,'Borstan\'s Meats? Is that for one of us?$B$BOh!$B$BWow... this smells really good! Yummy.$B$BThanks for bringing me my lunch. I can tell what Borstan is going to be serving daily when my friends and I walk the road to Grommash Hold, by the smells alone. This tastes like my favorite, the sweetglaze! But it\'s different. I like the strong-flavored crumbs.$B$BIf it\'s going to be this tasty every day, I think we need to stop our game to take our lunch together!',70790),
(97250,'So the rumors were true! I expected as much, tensions have been rising along the eastern coast for some time. I knew it would only be a matter of time before conflict crept into our territory.$B$BHowever, I am skeptical that we played a role in the tavern\'s destruction. Too many Horde civilians rely on that route for trade and travel. Perhaps you could investigate further if you find the time.$B$BIn any case, today\'s deed is a victory for the Horde, and a stern warning to the Alliance!',70862),
(97253,'Whooooa! Nice one, pal! You saved me from another one of Gagsprocket\'s unbearable lectures on the cost of metal. More importantly, I can jump right into building my next prototype.$B$BUhhh, I didn\'t have a reward planned... Do you like boxes?',70862),
(97279,'Thank you for returning these weapons, $N. I will get to work repairing them for the next wave of recruits.',70840),
(97281,'Woah, where did you find a neat thing like that? Ya know it reminds me of the other thing my boss Gazlowe always used to tell me...',70862),
(97282,'Hey, thanks pal! You\'ve been a really big help to me here and I appreciate it.$B$BHere\'s to hoping I can get this all charged up using these organs. I bet it\'ll make those no good harpies think twice about attacking my caravan again. I sure hope this works.$B$BEither way you\'ve done your side of the deal. Take this for your trouble.',70862),
(97288,'Oho! I believe I know this head. A cruel joke by our Dark Lady. A delicious one at that.$B$BI think I have a use for this.',70862),
(97289,'<The body twitches to life, panicking as it relives its final moments.>$B$BYou...',70790),
(97290,'Not cooperating, eh? Excellent. I always love a challenge.',70790),
(97291,'These will do nicely. We will see how much bravado our honored guest retains after he is subjected to my masterpiece.',70790),
(97292,'Excellent. We\'ll let his flesh simmer for awhile. Give him time to acclimate to his new home.$B$BI have no further use for the wretch for now, but we shall keep an eye on him. I have many plans for Othmar\'s future.',70790),
(97326,'How can you even hold all of those boulders!$B$BThose are great. Most even have a nice flat side, too. Now that you carried them all the way over here we can scoot them around in the dirt, right where we want \'em.$B$BThanks, $N!',70790),
(97485,'You have done well.$B$BI thank you for taking the time to perform one of our time-honored traditions, $r. I hope that as you travel you will find plenty of occasions you wish to give thanks for.$B$BShould you ever wish to perform the ritual again, you should be able to repurchase the components I sent you to collect.$B$BGo with An\'she\'s warmth.',70790),
(97538,'Ah, thank you, $N.$B$BIt means much to me to have you venture all the way out there for what must seem a trivial notion from an old tauren, but with your kindness I will have enough pigment for the rest of the season.$B$BThank you for supporting my livelihood, and I will strive to create something magnificent with the pigments you have brought.',70862),
(97539,'Splendid spider string. When you\'re being stitched back together, a little infection is the... least of your concerns.$B$BAhem, excuse me once again. Doctor humor.$B$BThanks for helping out the medical ward, $N. If only we could get this kind of help more regularly.',70862),
(97558,'Ah, excellent! Thank you for acquiring these. I can promise they will be put to good use.',70862),
(97583,'<The slime shudders with newfound energy. It seems to want to follow you, now that it has associated you with food.>',70790),
(97891,'Ah, marvelous! I had been waiting for Alessandro\'s potion to arrive. The last six he sent destabilized along the way, but you\'ve made it just in time!$B$BHere, take this for your effort. That is all for now, unless you have other business with me?$B$BIf not, remove yourself so I may continue my experiments unhindered.',70862),
(97904,'Dere ya have it, ya be craftin\' your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don\'t be carin\' much for camps being set up in da center of town, so ya be needin\' ta head into da wilderness if ya be wantin\' to try it out.$B$BNo camp is complete without a campfire, mon. Ya be needin\' one of dose before ya be startin\' up your camp. Most cooks be teachin\' ya ta make a fire. Check in with someone who can train ya in da culinary arts if ya haven\'t already learned da basics.',70790),
(97905,'Dere ya have it, ya be craftin\' your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don\'t be carin\' much for camps being set up in da center of town, so ya be needin\' ta head into da wilderness if ya be wantin\' to try it out.$B$BNo camp is complete without a campfire, mon. Ya be needin\' one of dose before ya be startin\' up your camp. Most cooks be teachin\' ya ta make a fire. Check in with someone who can train ya in da culinary arts if ya haven\'t already learned da basics.',70862),
(97907,'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.',70790),
(97908,'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.',70862),
(97924,'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.',70790),
(97946,'There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don\'t care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.',70790),
(97949,'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.',70790),
